1
00:02:04,008 --> 00:02:08,308
No living creature was
harmed during the filming.

2
00:02:08,971 --> 00:02:14,441
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:14,891 --> 00:02:17,211
The dogs of the one that set this trap.

4
00:02:18,231 --> 00:02:20,201
Come with your all.

5
00:02:20,273 --> 00:02:22,473
I will not leave any of you alive.

6
00:03:03,035 --> 00:03:04,715
Come. Come to me.

7
00:03:09,602 --> 00:03:11,942
Mother! Hold on, mother!

8
00:03:18,642 --> 00:03:20,552
Bala!

9
00:03:21,064 --> 00:03:22,594
I'll kill you now!

10
00:03:26,315 --> 00:03:28,395
Come. Come!

11
00:03:52,083 --> 00:03:56,083
It's the end of the road for you, Bala!

12
00:04:04,034 --> 00:04:05,714
Where did these people come?!

13
00:04:07,894 --> 00:04:10,454
Mother, hold on. Please.

14
00:04:39,607 --> 00:04:42,137
Mother, no.
No, please, hang on!

15
00:04:42,418 --> 00:04:44,028
No. No!

16
00:04:58,355 --> 00:05:01,305
You laugh like a hyena
that has seen a lion.

17
00:05:04,348 --> 00:05:05,988
Come.

18
00:05:06,656 --> 00:05:08,526
Come with your all!

19
00:05:24,986 --> 00:05:28,106
-We're here, Osman Bey!
-We're here to help, my Bey!

20
00:05:51,408 --> 00:05:52,564
Lions!

21
00:05:52,564 --> 00:05:54,920
-I know where they are.
-Let's get out of here.

22
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,960
Let's go.

23
00:06:22,219 --> 00:06:23,689
This way.

24
00:06:32,132 --> 00:06:34,282
Come on, quickly.

25
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:36,950
Hurry up.

26
00:06:57,427 --> 00:06:59,397
How great!

27
00:07:23,703 --> 00:07:26,037
Thank Allah, mother! Mother?

28
00:07:26,037 --> 00:07:29,067
Mother! No! Malhun!

29
00:07:33,649 --> 00:07:35,099
Bala!

30
00:07:41,653 --> 00:07:44,183
Soldiers! We are withdrawing!

31
00:07:54,212 --> 00:07:57,442
Who are you? Take off your covers!

32
00:08:01,742 --> 00:08:04,382
It's obvious that you are on
the right side.

33
00:08:05,212 --> 00:08:07,502
Mother! Mother!

34
00:08:07,523 --> 00:08:10,543
Mother! Wake up, mother!

35
00:08:12,299 --> 00:08:14,419
She is alive! She is alive!

36
00:08:14,674 --> 00:08:17,214
Come on! We're going!

37
00:08:17,327 --> 00:08:19,927
Mother, hang on! Please don't...

38
00:08:19,927 --> 00:08:21,557
leave me without you here!

39
00:08:47,749 --> 00:08:49,939
You were so good, Boran Alp.

40
00:08:51,336 --> 00:08:53,136
A valant was on the battlefield.

41
00:08:53,434 --> 00:08:55,734
Thank Allah we're on the right side.

42
00:08:55,837 --> 00:08:57,477
Thank you.

43
00:09:10,942 --> 00:09:13,462
Ask permission first.

44
00:09:13,669 --> 00:09:15,570
What do you want?

45
00:09:15,570 --> 00:09:17,890
-I need you to help me.
-Shut up.

46
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:21,340
Shut up! You're a snake next
to another snake.

47
00:09:21,676 --> 00:09:23,466
Why do you need my help?

48
00:09:23,466 --> 00:09:24,966
Julia.

49
00:09:26,969 --> 00:09:29,919
She will attack Hatuns. We
need to prevent this.

50
00:09:30,009 --> 00:09:33,549
What trap are you trying to lure me into?

51
00:09:35,019 --> 00:09:37,329
Did you make up for your previous
mistake...

52
00:09:37,548 --> 00:09:39,598
so that I can believe your word now?

53
00:09:39,952 --> 00:09:44,092
Boran, I saw my mistake and corrected it.

54
00:09:44,318 --> 00:09:47,948
But if you don't come with me now,
very bad things will happen. Come on.

55
00:09:51,369 --> 00:09:52,949
Are you on the right side?

56
00:09:56,512 --> 00:09:58,772
I'm both on the right side...

57
00:10:02,543 --> 00:10:04,913
and Osman Bey's side.

58
00:10:08,425 --> 00:10:10,295
Come on.

59
00:10:23,745 --> 00:10:27,235
Boran, what happened is
between you and me.

60
00:10:28,046 --> 00:10:29,716
It's a secret, Boran.

61
00:10:30,586 --> 00:10:33,626
If one of us gets in trouble, we'll help.

62
00:10:34,924 --> 00:10:36,384
Don't you--

63
00:10:38,735 --> 00:10:41,605
Only the one who receives
the secret knows the secret.

64
00:10:43,218 --> 00:10:45,738
I know that I shouldn't tell
this to anyone.

65
00:10:45,922 --> 00:10:47,822
Don't worry.

66
00:10:51,727 --> 00:10:54,067
Come on, let's go.

67
00:10:54,189 --> 00:10:56,919
Gündüz Bey is giving a feast
to celebrate his position.

68
00:10:56,984 --> 00:10:58,774
Let's go.

69
00:11:30,669 --> 00:11:33,639
Cevahir said there are other
shelters leading to the pass.

70
00:11:34,257 --> 00:11:36,137
We'll wait here.

71
00:11:36,137 --> 00:11:37,307
Alright.

72
00:11:38,213 --> 00:11:39,273
Let's go.

73
00:12:11,873 --> 00:12:14,484
I hesitate to say the grave situation...

74
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:17,304
but our Sultan's condition is not good.

75
00:12:19,627 --> 00:12:21,247
Osman came as a traitor.

76
00:12:22,046 --> 00:12:25,486
He did what was necessary and
intended to kill our Sultan.

77
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:31,140
He will be caught. Then, we'll ask
why he did this.

78
00:12:31,736 --> 00:12:35,026
Osman's trial will not take place and he
will be killed on sight.

79
00:12:44,389 --> 00:12:46,389
In the name of Allah.

80
00:12:47,449 --> 00:12:51,849
In the name of the 99 names of
Allah who make everything...

81
00:12:52,738 --> 00:12:55,988
happen with just one word and fill
our hearts with faith.

82
00:12:58,851 --> 00:13:01,961
My Beys, as you know...

83
00:13:03,089 --> 00:13:05,429
I aspire to be the Bey of Kayı Tribe.

84
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:17,793
A skillful Bey like you is suitable
to be the Bey of Kayı.

85
00:13:21,125 --> 00:13:25,271
Alright, Beys. Those who will vote for
Gündüz Bey,

86
00:13:25,271 --> 00:13:28,101
raise your hand.

87
00:13:53,926 --> 00:13:55,596
Is that so?

88
00:13:56,141 --> 00:14:00,971
So you prefer to be headless to
Gündüz Bey.

89
00:14:05,728 --> 00:14:10,138
So you are saying being headless
is better than him.

90
00:14:14,168 --> 00:14:15,528
Alright.

91
00:14:15,886 --> 00:14:20,046
Then, you will not take anything from
the conquests of Gündüz Bey.

92
00:14:23,719 --> 00:14:26,499
You will be deprived of a conqueror Bey.

93
00:14:32,915 --> 00:14:34,855
Say it, Gündüz Bey.

94
00:14:36,468 --> 00:14:40,968
Say what you couldn't say because
of your humility until this day.

95
00:14:45,839 --> 00:14:51,119
The property of the enemy, Harmankaya
Castle belongs to Kayı now.

96
00:14:59,616 --> 00:15:02,026
With the help of Vizier Alemşah...

97
00:15:03,439 --> 00:15:05,559
it will be the property of Kayı Tribe.

98
00:15:09,431 --> 00:15:10,891
It's wrong.

99
00:15:12,915 --> 00:15:15,335
Harmankaya is your property now.

100
00:15:17,037 --> 00:15:21,507
If you become the Bey of Kayı Tribe, it
will be the property of Kayı.

101
00:15:25,086 --> 00:15:28,626
Then, the Beys will get their share.

102
00:15:29,525 --> 00:15:32,785
They can sell their goods in
the markets of Harmankaya...

103
00:15:32,909 --> 00:15:35,839
and graze their animals on its lands.

104
00:15:36,913 --> 00:15:39,433
Many opportunities will be waiting
for them...

105
00:15:40,144 --> 00:15:42,494
and they will be revived in their tribe.

106
00:15:45,472 --> 00:15:47,372
I will repeat.

107
00:15:48,586 --> 00:15:53,646
Those who will vote for
Gündüz Bey, raise your hand.

108
00:16:28,426 --> 00:16:30,996
That's what they call trap.

109
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:35,650
Those bastards never stopped.

110
00:16:35,721 --> 00:16:39,461
They wanted to kill firstly Sultan Mesud
and then, me.

111
00:16:41,594 --> 00:16:43,794
My dagger is on the Sultan's back.

112
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:51,327
If they can't kill you, they will put the
blame of the Sultan's death on you.

113
00:17:09,363 --> 00:17:10,742
It's me, Cevahir.

114
00:17:20,711 --> 00:17:23,861
Come, my brother. It's up to
you from now on.

115
00:17:24,586 --> 00:17:26,746
We have big trouble.

116
00:17:26,952 --> 00:17:29,062
Get us out of the palace.

117
00:17:29,926 --> 00:17:32,926
I know your trouble, my brother.

118
00:17:44,306 --> 00:17:45,786
Cevahir!

119
00:17:45,831 --> 00:17:48,641
You used me and tried
to kill the Sultan.

120
00:17:49,628 --> 00:17:51,848
You made me a part of your treachery.

121
00:17:53,133 --> 00:17:54,713
I will make you surrender.

122
00:17:56,634 --> 00:17:58,204
What are you doing?

123
00:17:58,317 --> 00:18:01,667
You were my brother, Turgut! How could
you do this?

124
00:18:04,397 --> 00:18:07,674
Osman Bey, it's a black mark
on your name--

125
00:18:07,674 --> 00:18:09,254
Belt up!

126
00:18:18,090 --> 00:18:20,500
What do you know, Cevahir?

127
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:28,680
What do you know?

128
00:18:31,025 --> 00:18:34,155
Are you trying to
tarnish my name?

129
00:18:41,404 --> 00:18:43,404
Look at my eyes.

130
00:18:44,973 --> 00:18:46,793
Do you see a traitor?

131
00:18:50,928 --> 00:18:53,078
Sultan Mesud's aide...

132
00:18:53,781 --> 00:18:56,451
tried to kill him in the first place.

133
00:18:57,309 --> 00:18:59,189
And then, he tried to kill me.

134
00:19:05,226 --> 00:19:07,306
He got what he deserved.

135
00:19:07,899 --> 00:19:10,369
But I couldn't protect the Sultan.

136
00:19:11,039 --> 00:19:14,099
It's a game of Geyhatu and Vizier
Alemşah.

137
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:25,800
You don't have a fault, Cevahir.

138
00:19:25,906 --> 00:19:30,706
But those bastards want to ruin the
reputation of Osman Bey and Kayı Tribe.

139
00:19:31,381 --> 00:19:33,711
Trust your brother Turgut.

140
00:19:36,689 --> 00:19:39,299
What if it's a part of your plan?

141
00:19:47,270 --> 00:19:49,960
Do I look like I'm planning something?

142
00:19:56,083 --> 00:19:57,983
Tell me.

143
00:20:01,794 --> 00:20:03,284
Put down your swords.

144
00:20:28,579 --> 00:20:30,779
Why don't you talk, Kumral Abdal?

145
00:20:30,976 --> 00:20:33,416
Tell us if she will be alright or not?

146
00:20:35,075 --> 00:20:37,245
There's always hope.

147
00:20:41,204 --> 00:20:43,544
But her wound is so deep.

148
00:20:45,424 --> 00:20:46,954
So deep.

149
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:00,100
Kumral Abdal.

150
00:21:04,158 --> 00:21:05,578
I made syrup.

151
00:21:07,885 --> 00:21:09,505
May Allah give healing.

152
00:21:10,833 --> 00:21:12,843
Thank you.

153
00:21:21,826 --> 00:21:23,876
In the name of Allah.

154
00:21:39,851 --> 00:21:41,461
It's because of me.

155
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:43,810
If she hadn't jumped in front of me...

156
00:21:44,527 --> 00:21:46,907
Don't do this, Bala. You did nothing
wrong.

157
00:21:48,584 --> 00:21:50,744
Also, Selcan Hatun is strong.

158
00:21:50,915 --> 00:21:52,495
She will be alright.

159
00:21:53,313 --> 00:21:56,773
Yes, she is strong. She is the mother of
Kayı Tribe.

160
00:21:57,112 --> 00:21:58,792
She is strong.

161
00:22:00,635 --> 00:22:03,885
My Allah, don't take our mother from us.

162
00:22:05,063 --> 00:22:06,173
Amen.

163
00:22:17,948 --> 00:22:18,928
Mother!

164
00:22:20,160 --> 00:22:21,690
Mother?

165
00:22:22,160 --> 00:22:24,830
-Mother?
-Mother Selcan?

166
00:22:25,633 --> 00:22:27,693
Mother.

167
00:22:30,824 --> 00:22:32,194
Mother.

168
00:22:34,338 --> 00:22:37,458
We're okay, mother.
Thanks to you, we're alright.

169
00:22:37,698 --> 00:22:39,208
You'll be alright too.

170
00:22:40,840 --> 00:22:42,930
Thank Allah.

171
00:22:54,495 --> 00:22:57,365
It's good that there are good
and brave men like...

172
00:22:58,035 --> 00:22:59,915
you in Konya, which is writhing...

173
00:23:00,359 --> 00:23:02,649
in the clutches of traitors.

174
00:23:06,832 --> 00:23:08,692
We'll get out of this palace.

175
00:23:08,692 --> 00:23:12,692
Osman Bey, there's no possibility to leave
the palace under the cover of a merchant.

176
00:23:14,077 --> 00:23:15,937
Everywhere is full of soldiers.

177
00:23:16,787 --> 00:23:21,107
He is right. It is hard to leave
the palace in this situation.

178
00:23:21,969 --> 00:23:24,299
Every hard thing has an easy way to do.

179
00:23:25,751 --> 00:23:28,341
They wouldn't keep the
carcasses of these dogs...

180
00:23:30,456 --> 00:23:32,466
we killed in the palace, would they?

181
00:23:41,178 --> 00:23:46,258
The enemy was not able to harm us
thanks to two brave men.

182
00:23:47,832 --> 00:23:49,522
May Allah bless them.

183
00:23:50,499 --> 00:23:52,449
Who are those valants?

184
00:23:52,599 --> 00:23:56,589
Their faces were covered, that's why we
have no idea, my Sheik.

185
00:23:58,513 --> 00:24:01,913
We don't know but Allah does.

186
00:24:02,969 --> 00:24:06,809
But with the one whose
heart is with us...

187
00:24:07,496 --> 00:24:09,376
our hearts are one.

188
00:24:11,672 --> 00:24:15,682
Whoever is a hypocrite, who wants
to kill us...

189
00:24:15,954 --> 00:24:18,644
who sheds innocent people's
blood, we are...

190
00:24:19,529 --> 00:24:22,849
far away from him until
the Day of Judgment.

191
00:24:23,652 --> 00:24:27,852
But the Sword that wraps around
my daughters' neck is Nikola.

192
00:24:28,550 --> 00:24:30,950
So, the Vizier holds its hilt.

193
00:24:32,914 --> 00:24:37,274
Vizier Alemşah has given up the
right way for falsehood...

194
00:24:37,554 --> 00:24:40,904
and changed guidance with perversion.

195
00:24:42,474 --> 00:24:44,314
Hypocrites.

196
00:24:47,773 --> 00:24:49,863
Hypocrites.

197
00:24:52,905 --> 00:24:54,275
"Hypocrites...

198
00:24:55,465 --> 00:24:57,255
are deaf...

199
00:24:58,569 --> 00:25:00,339
dumb...

200
00:25:02,501 --> 00:25:04,311
and blind.

201
00:25:06,112 --> 00:25:08,622
They will not choose the right
way anymore."

202
00:25:14,290 --> 00:25:19,250
The one who truly deserves the hide
is the one who never wants it.

203
00:25:21,026 --> 00:25:22,766
Beys witnessed that...

204
00:25:23,486 --> 00:25:26,796
Gündüz Bey waived his right in the past.

205
00:25:26,802 --> 00:25:30,337
Although he was the biggest, he waived
his right, we are witness to this.

206
00:25:30,337 --> 00:25:31,857
Yes, we are.

207
00:25:31,995 --> 00:25:37,375
The order that I am talking about
is only possible with the conquest.

208
00:25:38,376 --> 00:25:43,106
You will follow Gündüz Bey until
the enemy...

209
00:25:43,718 --> 00:25:46,838
leave this land, Beys.

210
00:25:51,404 --> 00:25:53,554
It's impossible for you to stop now.

211
00:25:55,989 --> 00:26:02,889
But first, our tribes will be blessed with
the trophy from Harmankaya.

212
00:26:04,103 --> 00:26:06,333
You are saying great things, Vizier...

213
00:26:06,689 --> 00:26:08,489
but what about Osman Bey?

214
00:26:09,475 --> 00:26:11,815
What will happen when he turns back?

215
00:26:15,598 --> 00:26:19,948
Osman Bey is one of the
greatest valants of this land.

216
00:26:21,318 --> 00:26:25,218
Sultan Mesud will forgive him...

217
00:26:26,732 --> 00:26:28,892
when his anger is ceased.

218
00:26:30,459 --> 00:26:32,219
I hope so.

219
00:26:33,058 --> 00:26:34,928
Can I come in, my Bey?

220
00:26:35,360 --> 00:26:37,120
Come.

221
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:43,530
There is news from Konya.

222
00:26:43,875 --> 00:26:45,395
Osman Bey...

223
00:26:46,867 --> 00:26:49,427
escaped when he was taken to Konya.

224
00:26:49,936 --> 00:26:53,326
Also, he killed Sergeant İlgezdi and
many Seljuk soldiers.

225
00:26:56,323 --> 00:26:59,933
One of his alps, Göktüğ was martyred
when they were running away.

226
00:27:14,258 --> 00:27:16,068
Göktüğ.

227
00:27:16,245 --> 00:27:18,325
The valant of Kayı, Göktüğ.

228
00:27:20,358 --> 00:27:22,268
Göktuğ.

229
00:27:24,375 --> 00:27:26,185
My brother.

230
00:27:27,870 --> 00:27:29,580
Göktüğ!

231
00:27:32,810 --> 00:27:35,170
You.. you...

232
00:27:38,648 --> 00:27:40,538
What are you saying?

233
00:27:41,690 --> 00:27:44,130
What do you mean by Göktüğ is dead?!

234
00:27:44,269 --> 00:27:46,189
What are you talking about?!

235
00:27:56,659 --> 00:27:58,749
Vizier.

236
00:27:59,159 --> 00:28:00,959
Vizier...

237
00:28:06,666 --> 00:28:09,216
my brother died because of you.

238
00:28:16,450 --> 00:28:18,740
You brought death here.

239
00:28:22,774 --> 00:28:25,094
And you will go by death.

240
00:28:25,968 --> 00:28:27,798
Vizier.

241
00:28:30,733 --> 00:28:32,213
Boran!

242
00:28:44,363 --> 00:28:46,083
I said Boran!

243
00:28:48,301 --> 00:28:51,701
What do you think you are doing by
glowering at the Vizier...

244
00:28:51,701 --> 00:28:53,611
in the presence of your Bey?

245
00:28:59,367 --> 00:29:01,007
It's enough, Boran.

246
00:29:02,270 --> 00:29:04,720
Behave yourself.

247
00:29:14,469 --> 00:29:15,919
Now...

248
00:29:16,171 --> 00:29:17,651
get out of my sight!

249
00:29:51,488 --> 00:29:53,358
Osman Bey.

250
00:29:54,638 --> 00:29:58,008
You are doing wrong things...

251
00:29:58,591 --> 00:30:01,321
while we hope you will be forgiven.

252
00:30:04,806 --> 00:30:07,366
I knew Sergeant İlgezdi.

253
00:30:08,614 --> 00:30:10,754
He was such a lion.

254
00:30:13,132 --> 00:30:16,662
Osman is now on a road of no return.

255
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:23,170
Beys, as choosing Gündüz Bey as your
leader...

256
00:30:23,300 --> 00:30:25,390
...you did what's best.

257
00:30:56,059 --> 00:30:58,089
Give me some good news, Ferman.

258
00:31:00,669 --> 00:31:01,939
My Bey...

259
00:31:03,041 --> 00:31:07,421
...two men with their faces covered
failed all our moves.

260
00:31:08,713 --> 00:31:10,923
But Selcen Hatun is heavily wounded.

261
00:31:11,752 --> 00:31:13,692
Nos she is at the lodge.

262
00:31:14,519 --> 00:31:17,129
But Selcen is heavily wounded.

263
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:24,060
So, all those men were beaten by two
face covered bandits...

264
00:31:24,484 --> 00:31:26,454
...is that so?

265
00:31:28,137 --> 00:31:29,907
Can't you just...

266
00:31:30,734 --> 00:31:35,554
...succeed at one job when I am
not around...

267
00:31:35,829 --> 00:31:38,099
...Ferman?

268
00:31:40,583 --> 00:31:42,493
This is not over.

269
00:31:44,316 --> 00:31:48,336
But first, I will see Geyhatu.

270
00:31:49,518 --> 00:31:52,168
We will take care of the hatuns
eventually.

271
00:32:15,401 --> 00:32:17,371
Commander Onat's order!

272
00:32:17,710 --> 00:32:20,030
Not even a bird will fly around!

273
00:32:20,189 --> 00:32:23,339
No one will leave Konya without
reporting!

274
00:32:26,521 --> 00:32:28,021
Come on!

275
00:32:29,130 --> 00:32:30,780
Wait!

276
00:32:31,614 --> 00:32:33,914
I am saying not a bird will fly.

277
00:32:34,378 --> 00:32:36,088
Where is this carriage going?

278
00:32:46,509 --> 00:32:48,289
What does it carry?

279
00:32:48,672 --> 00:32:51,122
It carries the men Osman killed.

280
00:32:52,044 --> 00:32:54,434
Commander Onat's orders.

281
00:32:57,351 --> 00:33:00,141
If you want to see a dead body,
uncover it.

282
00:33:01,653 --> 00:33:04,073
It is fine. Take it!

283
00:33:07,967 --> 00:33:09,507
Let's go!

284
00:33:25,018 --> 00:33:26,868
Follow that carriage!

285
00:33:57,541 --> 00:33:58,681
Mother!

286
00:34:22,545 --> 00:34:23,844
Is she all right?

287
00:34:26,411 --> 00:34:28,101
If anything happens to my mother...

288
00:34:31,099 --> 00:34:33,049
...I will come for you.

289
00:34:35,463 --> 00:34:37,813
Look what you have caused,
Gündüz Bey!

290
00:34:38,052 --> 00:34:40,121
Look carefully.

291
00:34:41,114 --> 00:34:42,525
How did it happen?

292
00:34:44,661 --> 00:34:46,442
Tell me.

293
00:34:46,731 --> 00:34:48,281
Who did this?

294
00:34:48,509 --> 00:34:51,518
Who could?
Those you work with did it.

295
00:34:52,081 --> 00:34:56,871
Whoever will benefit from our death
did it.

296
00:35:01,284 --> 00:35:02,974
Julia.

297
00:35:05,813 --> 00:35:08,383
The dog of that Nikola...

298
00:35:08,844 --> 00:35:10,574
...whom you work with.

299
00:35:10,574 --> 00:35:13,634
But not only Nikola is behind this.

300
00:35:14,699 --> 00:35:17,839
You know whom we bother well,
Gündüz Bey.

301
00:35:18,252 --> 00:35:21,082
Vizier Alemşah sent that dog after us.

302
00:35:22,356 --> 00:35:27,286
Aren't you tired of blaming Alemşah for
everything that happens to you?

303
00:35:33,362 --> 00:35:35,662
You know it better, Gündüz Bey.

304
00:35:36,480 --> 00:35:38,810
Vizier and Nikola share a goal.

305
00:36:16,994 --> 00:36:18,414
Mother.

306
00:36:21,358 --> 00:36:23,458
I will not let them get away with this.

307
00:36:24,117 --> 00:36:26,837
Did you just remember that I was your
mother?

308
00:36:28,667 --> 00:36:31,087
You exiled me from my tribe.

309
00:36:33,772 --> 00:36:35,202
Mother.

310
00:36:35,931 --> 00:36:39,161
You didn't listen to your mother's words.

311
00:36:40,667 --> 00:36:42,587
You didn't just lose me...

312
00:36:43,176 --> 00:36:46,336
...you lost what your brother entrusted
to you.

313
00:36:47,916 --> 00:36:50,996
You separated a mother from her child.

314
00:36:52,059 --> 00:36:53,399
Tell me.

315
00:36:54,910 --> 00:36:56,590
Who are you?

316
00:37:00,627 --> 00:37:04,067
We now have full control over Kayı Tribe.

317
00:37:04,717 --> 00:37:09,507
Their new Bey, Gündüz, listens to
everything I say.

318
00:37:10,767 --> 00:37:11,877
Good.

319
00:37:17,061 --> 00:37:20,111
Osman tried to kill the Sultan.

320
00:37:22,388 --> 00:37:23,968
He is a traitor now.

321
00:37:25,407 --> 00:37:28,027
Konya will be his grave.

322
00:37:30,141 --> 00:37:32,761
They say Sultan is not in good condition.

323
00:37:33,753 --> 00:37:35,683
What if he dies?

324
00:37:36,576 --> 00:37:39,246
We will mourn, Alemşah.

325
00:37:39,422 --> 00:37:40,562
We will mourn

326
00:37:44,562 --> 00:37:48,362
His youngest son will become the Sultan.

327
00:37:50,797 --> 00:37:55,287
The kid will listen to our orders.

328
00:37:57,136 --> 00:38:02,426
Our moves have worked both in
orient and western.

329
00:38:03,193 --> 00:38:07,193
Gündüz will take Harmankaya from Nikola.

330
00:38:08,004 --> 00:38:09,564
This is the first move.

331
00:38:10,650 --> 00:38:15,130
Later, İznik and every land around it...

332
00:38:15,516 --> 00:38:16,996
...will be ours.

333
00:38:18,158 --> 00:38:20,338
With the power I gathered from there...

334
00:38:20,602 --> 00:38:24,602
...I will establish a huge army...

335
00:38:24,722 --> 00:38:27,692
... consisting of Greeks, Turks,
and Mongols.

336
00:38:28,522 --> 00:38:30,292
With this army...

337
00:38:30,451 --> 00:38:35,701
...I will dethrone Argun Han, the ruler of
the Mongols.

338
00:38:37,343 --> 00:38:39,073
I will sit on that throne.

339
00:38:39,454 --> 00:38:40,924
Me.

340
00:38:43,868 --> 00:38:46,178
You will sit on that throne.

341
00:38:47,324 --> 00:38:49,984
Although they don't call me Sultan...

342
00:38:50,538 --> 00:38:54,338
...I will be controlling
the whole Seljuk.

343
00:38:57,792 --> 00:39:00,472
Osman is the only obstacle...

344
00:39:00,755 --> 00:39:02,605
...for this.

345
00:39:03,187 --> 00:39:05,177
Osman will die.

346
00:39:14,381 --> 00:39:16,301
Where are you, Osman Bey?

347
00:39:17,794 --> 00:39:19,514
Where are you?

348
00:39:31,762 --> 00:39:33,162
Finally.

349
00:39:48,139 --> 00:39:50,359
-Kosses!
-Finally!

350
00:40:19,080 --> 00:40:20,370
Osman!

351
00:40:21,764 --> 00:40:23,054
Where are you going?

352
00:40:23,431 --> 00:40:25,241
So you are looking for me!

353
00:40:27,673 --> 00:40:31,973
You are one of those looming over the
Seljuk like a nightmare!

354
00:40:33,294 --> 00:40:35,914
Your end will be like your allies!

355
00:40:36,461 --> 00:40:39,051
Now I will loom over you like a nightmare,
Osman!

356
00:40:39,907 --> 00:40:41,967
Come here!

357
00:40:42,081 --> 00:40:43,781
Come!

358
00:41:47,055 --> 00:41:50,985
Osman, you first defeated Selman.

359
00:41:51,169 --> 00:41:54,819
You escaped before they kill you there.
That dagger is for you!

360
00:41:55,735 --> 00:41:58,902
You and your tribe will be remembered
as traitors when you die!

361
00:42:04,631 --> 00:42:06,931
Allah will show what he sees to his
subjects!

362
00:42:07,881 --> 00:42:09,401
Go, Osman Bey!

363
00:42:09,422 --> 00:42:12,332
Our honor spreads from tongue to tongue!

364
00:42:16,417 --> 00:42:19,307
The whole world knows Osman!

365
00:42:20,671 --> 00:42:22,891
Don't worry!

366
00:42:37,315 --> 00:42:40,395
Cevahir!
Cevahir!

367
00:42:49,456 --> 00:42:51,026
Cevahir!

368
00:42:51,823 --> 00:42:53,753
Cevahir!
Brother!

369
00:42:54,341 --> 00:42:56,381
Oh, my brother!

370
00:42:56,532 --> 00:42:58,222
My brother!

371
00:42:59,060 --> 00:43:00,910
A valiant dies...

372
00:43:00,955 --> 00:43:03,785
...but his name remains.
You fought like a valiant, brother.

373
00:43:04,044 --> 00:43:06,394
Go to out Allah with peace.

374
00:43:06,547 --> 00:43:07,667
Brother!

375
00:43:10,185 --> 00:43:12,955
I go to my Rabb's presence with
the comfort of...

376
00:43:14,666 --> 00:43:16,886
...dying on the right path.

377
00:43:20,229 --> 00:43:22,239
"I bear witness...

378
00:44:07,170 --> 00:44:09,240
Allah is the greatest!

379
00:44:10,088 --> 00:44:11,968
Allah is the greatest!

380
00:44:13,405 --> 00:44:15,405
Allah is the greatest!

381
00:44:29,260 --> 00:44:31,180
My end is here...

382
00:44:31,366 --> 00:44:33,446
...but yours is not far either!

383
00:44:45,490 --> 00:44:48,030
Allah!
Allah!

384
00:44:53,642 --> 00:44:56,582
Mashallah, Solgur Agha!

385
00:44:57,083 --> 00:45:00,573
You screamed once and you put fear
in the heart of the oppressors.

386
00:45:02,246 --> 00:45:04,561
You killed them like a hunter, mashallah.

387
00:45:04,561 --> 00:45:06,347
They call me the lion hunter.

388
00:45:07,117 --> 00:45:10,547
When I heard that dog call you Osman
I came.

389
00:45:10,657 --> 00:45:14,197
Thank you, but you had to kill
dogs today...

390
00:45:14,775 --> 00:45:16,475
...instead of lions.

391
00:45:16,905 --> 00:45:18,274
Thank you.

392
00:45:18,274 --> 00:45:22,924
If you ever have a problem in Konya, no
matter where I am, I will come.

393
00:45:23,298 --> 00:45:24,828
Thank you.

394
00:45:24,828 --> 00:45:26,898
Thank you too, Osman Bey.

395
00:45:27,607 --> 00:45:29,317
Praise be!

396
00:45:30,413 --> 00:45:32,383
Are you the son...

397
00:45:33,099 --> 00:45:36,669
...Halime Hatun raised with a great
care?

398
00:45:37,948 --> 00:45:40,988
If they knew you turned your back on
your brother...

399
00:45:41,429 --> 00:45:44,849
...what would your mother, father say?
Have you ever thought about this?

400
00:45:45,530 --> 00:45:47,040
Don't do this, mother.

401
00:45:48,585 --> 00:45:51,195
I didn't turn my back on my brother.

402
00:45:51,260 --> 00:45:53,990
You know, I always envied you.

403
00:45:54,863 --> 00:45:58,863
What a good son Halime Hatun has raised,
I said.

404
00:45:59,271 --> 00:46:02,841
He got his brother's back.
Cares for him like a mother...

405
00:46:03,074 --> 00:46:05,884
...I said.

406
00:46:06,323 --> 00:46:08,453
Don't say that, mother.

407
00:46:10,426 --> 00:46:12,796
I am still on my brother's side.

408
00:46:17,453 --> 00:46:19,663
Ask here.

409
00:46:23,825 --> 00:46:25,835
Which side?

410
00:46:28,706 --> 00:46:31,236
There is a story.

411
00:46:32,073 --> 00:46:35,693
They were beating a man.

412
00:46:36,474 --> 00:46:39,544
They were hitting his chest.

413
00:46:39,852 --> 00:46:44,142
But the man was crying
''My back, my back!''.

414
00:46:47,550 --> 00:46:51,500
Finally, they stopped and asked.

415
00:46:51,591 --> 00:46:54,391
''We are hitting your chest...

416
00:46:54,529 --> 00:46:57,749
...Why are you crying for your back?''

417
00:47:00,963 --> 00:47:03,173
Do you know what he said?

418
00:47:05,516 --> 00:47:08,826
He said, ''If my back was tough,
protected...

419
00:47:09,181 --> 00:47:11,691
...you wouldn't be able to hit my chest.''

420
00:47:13,925 --> 00:47:17,245
A brother protects your back.

421
00:47:21,085 --> 00:47:22,842
Go, sit on your throne.

422
00:47:27,441 --> 00:47:28,811
Come on.

423
00:47:48,480 --> 00:47:50,890
Bless your right to me, mother.

424
00:48:10,175 --> 00:48:12,755
I don't want to see you anymore.

425
00:48:13,468 --> 00:48:15,188
Go.

426
00:48:18,889 --> 00:48:21,139
I have no right on you as a mother.

427
00:48:22,150 --> 00:48:24,010
But know that...

428
00:48:25,002 --> 00:48:29,002
...I will pray as your aunt until my
last breath...

429
00:48:29,281 --> 00:48:32,181
...for you to see what is right.

430
00:49:41,509 --> 00:49:42,999
My Sheik.

431
00:49:58,036 --> 00:50:00,056
My Sheik, my heart is burning.

432
00:50:01,578 --> 00:50:03,378
My heart is burning, my Sheik.

433
00:50:05,657 --> 00:50:08,257
Would I ever do this if I knew this
would happen?

434
00:50:08,279 --> 00:50:12,419
If you knew and you did, you would be
an oppressor.

435
00:50:13,134 --> 00:50:17,204
You are one of the heedless for
doing it unknowingly.

436
00:50:18,305 --> 00:50:20,145
For the sake of my tribe...

437
00:50:21,310 --> 00:50:23,190
...for the sake of all of us!

438
00:50:23,724 --> 00:50:26,254
I wanted to expel the hatuns not to shed
blood.

439
00:50:27,037 --> 00:50:30,697
They would of course return when I
set an order, my Sheik.

440
00:50:33,701 --> 00:50:35,791
I didn't want this to happen.

441
00:50:35,823 --> 00:50:38,973
A Muslim should be wise.

442
00:50:39,691 --> 00:50:43,691
He should always be cautious, Gündüz Bey.

443
00:50:46,248 --> 00:50:50,188
Do you know the infidels who built
Mescid-i Dırar?

444
00:50:52,229 --> 00:50:54,819
Their aim was to cause discord
among believers...

445
00:50:55,817 --> 00:50:58,807
...and to help those who were
hostile to Allah...

446
00:50:59,128 --> 00:51:01,218
...and the Prophet.

447
00:51:02,128 --> 00:51:06,698
They wanted to paint the nest of betrayal
and sin...

448
00:51:07,077 --> 00:51:09,157
...as Allah's home.

449
00:51:10,601 --> 00:51:14,561
But nothing is a secret to our Allah.

450
00:51:17,038 --> 00:51:22,338
He is the one hearing and seeing all.

451
00:51:25,671 --> 00:51:29,511
He informed the prophet of their intention
in Surah At-Tawba.

452
00:51:30,844 --> 00:51:36,014
It was forbidden to come to
the presence of Allah...

453
00:51:36,804 --> 00:51:40,084
...in the evil house,
that so-called mosque.

454
00:51:41,188 --> 00:51:46,348
The Prophet of Allah immediately
destroyed that nest of discord.

455
00:51:48,554 --> 00:51:53,544
The verses of Allah and the Sunnah
of His Prophet are obvious.

456
00:51:55,670 --> 00:51:58,940
Do you think those hypocrites who built
Mescid-i Dırar...

457
00:51:59,703 --> 00:52:03,113
...are today doing nothing, Gündüz Bey?

458
00:52:04,403 --> 00:52:05,863
They don't.

459
00:52:07,009 --> 00:52:11,949
But the heedless prostrate themselves
in the taverns...

460
00:52:12,619 --> 00:52:14,779
...and palaces of the hypocrites today.

461
00:52:15,469 --> 00:52:19,159
They don't destroy them Gündüz Bey.

462
00:52:21,299 --> 00:52:24,429
We are always against those hypocrites,
my Sheik.

463
00:52:26,683 --> 00:52:29,533
But, I see that...

464
00:52:30,624 --> 00:52:33,404
...you blame Alemşah for every evil too.

465
00:52:34,257 --> 00:52:36,707
I vouch for his intentions, my Sheik.

466
00:52:37,179 --> 00:52:39,359
He thinks for the sake of the Turks.

467
00:52:39,727 --> 00:52:41,667
Vizier Alemşah...

468
00:52:42,041 --> 00:52:48,641
...sealed your eyes, your ears and
your heart with evil so badly that...

469
00:52:49,441 --> 00:52:54,001
...you haven't been able to wake up for
so long.

470
00:52:56,253 --> 00:53:00,253
The end of those who persist in
heedlessness is hypocrisy.

471
00:53:01,465 --> 00:53:05,325
Obviously, my word means nothing to you.

472
00:53:16,273 --> 00:53:18,063
Gündüz Bey...

473
00:53:18,970 --> 00:53:21,920
...if you ever wish to wake up...

474
00:53:23,503 --> 00:53:28,453
...be a disciple of your conscience,
a guide to your soul.

475
00:53:43,931 --> 00:53:46,311
Everything is clear and obvious.

476
00:53:48,820 --> 00:53:53,310
Vizier Alemşah and Geyhatu are working
together.

477
00:53:53,448 --> 00:53:55,418
That is clear.

478
00:53:57,235 --> 00:54:00,715
But, what will we do now?

479
00:54:00,898 --> 00:54:02,978
What to do is certain.

480
00:54:03,189 --> 00:54:07,369
Sultan Mesud also needs to see they
work together.

481
00:54:08,298 --> 00:54:09,498
We do.

482
00:54:10,704 --> 00:54:14,464
But they are so good at deceiving.

483
00:54:14,569 --> 00:54:16,479
Do we know...

484
00:54:16,967 --> 00:54:20,397
...if Sultan Mesid is alive or dead?

485
00:54:22,413 --> 00:54:24,463
I hope he is alive.

486
00:54:26,702 --> 00:54:28,122
If he dies...

487
00:54:29,956 --> 00:54:33,546
...all this will get even worse.

488
00:54:34,094 --> 00:54:35,824
Let's pray he lives.

489
00:54:36,302 --> 00:54:38,462
Otherwise seems terrible.

490
00:54:39,103 --> 00:54:41,893
I've spent so much time with Sultan Mesud.

491
00:54:42,002 --> 00:54:44,042
He is a strong man.

492
00:54:44,305 --> 00:54:45,655
He is made of steel.

493
00:54:46,393 --> 00:54:49,233
-He will recover.
-I hope.

494
00:54:50,413 --> 00:54:53,203
Sultan will recover for sure but...

495
00:54:55,323 --> 00:54:57,763
...how are we going to heal these
wounds, Osman?

496
00:55:00,387 --> 00:55:02,607
They took your tribe.

497
00:55:02,957 --> 00:55:04,797
They took my castle.

498
00:55:05,504 --> 00:55:08,314
Both of our states know us as traitors.

499
00:55:10,003 --> 00:55:12,423
Tell me, what are we going to do now?

500
00:55:18,344 --> 00:55:20,754
Understanding what I am about to
say...

501
00:55:23,036 --> 00:55:25,136
...will be hard for you, Kosses.

502
00:55:27,287 --> 00:55:31,637
Is the property ours to be sad when
we lose it?

503
00:55:34,520 --> 00:55:36,590
The property belongs only to Allah.

504
00:55:41,349 --> 00:55:43,469
My tribe is a vehicle for me.

505
00:55:44,007 --> 00:55:47,447
I burn with love to glorify it.

506
00:55:47,976 --> 00:55:50,536
This is my only aim.

507
00:55:52,063 --> 00:55:55,103
Let them know us how they want to.

508
00:55:56,694 --> 00:56:00,534
Our intention is pure, our way is
the right way.

509
00:56:01,062 --> 00:56:02,792
Thank you.

510
00:56:04,136 --> 00:56:07,656
So your tribe is not liable to you,
you are liable to your tribe?

511
00:56:11,625 --> 00:56:13,735
Do you share his opinion, Turgut?

512
00:56:14,022 --> 00:56:19,002
If we had şeft everything behind and
spent the night in this cave...

513
00:56:20,237 --> 00:56:22,547
...sure we share the same opinion.

514
00:56:23,150 --> 00:56:25,830
But my only worry is...

515
00:56:26,907 --> 00:56:28,087
...Mari.

516
00:56:32,562 --> 00:56:34,512
Mari is a very strong girl.

517
00:56:36,255 --> 00:56:38,885
He learned how to fight from his brother.

518
00:56:39,685 --> 00:56:41,165
Thank you.

519
00:56:42,530 --> 00:56:44,930
Also, Kayı's hatuns are with her.

520
00:56:45,673 --> 00:56:48,643
They will protect each other, right,
Osman Bey?

521
00:56:48,676 --> 00:56:51,066
They will protect each other.

522
00:56:52,984 --> 00:56:54,994
And we will protect each other.

523
00:56:59,489 --> 00:57:02,989
May my Allah grant us fighting for
the same cause together.

524
00:57:03,680 --> 00:57:05,150
Amen.

525
00:57:08,553 --> 00:57:13,883
After I get my castle, I will continue
to my way, Osman Bey.

526
00:57:17,589 --> 00:57:22,479
You know, my enmity with you goes back
a long time.

527
00:57:24,257 --> 00:57:26,517
Fate opens such doors that...

528
00:57:28,699 --> 00:57:31,189
...it is not known who will be friends
with whom...

529
00:57:32,349 --> 00:57:35,759
...and who will be enemies.

530
00:57:39,359 --> 00:57:41,479
If you are here with me now...

531
00:57:42,822 --> 00:57:45,272
...there sure is a reason.

532
00:58:01,842 --> 00:58:04,542
My Sultan!
Thank goodness!

533
00:58:26,399 --> 00:58:30,659
Who did this to me?

534
00:58:32,069 --> 00:58:34,249
Osman, my Sultan.

535
00:58:35,734 --> 00:58:37,954
Osman!

536
00:58:42,423 --> 00:58:44,823
Osman has escaped the palace.

537
00:58:44,846 --> 00:58:46,686
He is searched everywhere.

538
00:58:46,686 --> 00:58:48,896
It is said that he left Konya.

539
00:58:49,501 --> 00:58:51,891
Sultan is still alive.

540
00:58:52,028 --> 00:58:54,178
Osman!

541
00:58:54,589 --> 00:58:57,209
You got away again huh?

542
00:58:57,729 --> 00:59:01,209
I will get your head, for sure.

543
00:59:03,898 --> 00:59:06,348
Gündüz Bey, the Bey of Kayı is here!

544
00:59:06,473 --> 00:59:07,813
Let him in!

545
00:59:18,197 --> 00:59:20,337
Welcome, Gündüz Bey.

546
00:59:23,160 --> 00:59:25,280
I wish to speak with you alone.

547
00:59:39,021 --> 00:59:42,421
Who did this treacherous attack...

548
00:59:43,075 --> 00:59:44,715
...on the hatuns...

549
00:59:46,537 --> 00:59:48,257
...Vizier Alemşah?

550
00:59:51,461 --> 00:59:53,251
I've heard.

551
00:59:54,347 --> 00:59:57,367
I sent soldiers there as soon as I heard.

552
00:59:58,985 --> 01:00:01,125
It is said that Julia had done it.

553
01:00:02,184 --> 01:00:04,404
It is obvious that this is Nikola's doing.

554
01:00:07,377 --> 01:00:09,087
Slime bag!

555
01:00:09,395 --> 01:00:11,975
He is only strong enough
to mess with hatuns.

556
01:00:17,034 --> 01:00:18,574
Nikola huh?

557
01:00:19,998 --> 01:00:22,798
He shed the blood of Mother Selcan huh!?

558
01:00:24,448 --> 01:00:27,148
As soon as he leaves that castle...

559
01:00:27,917 --> 01:00:30,287
...I know exactly what to do to him.

560
01:00:31,935 --> 01:00:33,925
Vizier Alam Shah,...

561
01:00:34,287 --> 01:00:36,747
...I will rally the entire Turkmen.

562
01:00:36,956 --> 01:00:39,236
There is no need for that, Güzdüz Bey.

563
01:00:40,094 --> 01:00:45,904
Tomorrow, the ones that take
Harmankaya will pay a heavy price.

564
01:00:48,005 --> 01:00:52,645
Tonight, I will head to where Nikola is.

565
01:00:53,928 --> 01:00:55,868
I will divert him.

566
01:00:56,327 --> 01:01:00,657
And you, by morning, will conquer
Harmankaya with you alps.

567
01:01:03,623 --> 01:01:08,193
But anything can be expected from Nikola.

568
01:01:09,228 --> 01:01:12,198
Take Turkmen Beys with you as well...

569
01:01:13,114 --> 01:01:15,744
...so that they can't stand in your way.

570
01:01:16,408 --> 01:01:20,688
Have them earn all that loot.

571
01:01:25,459 --> 01:01:29,209
Harmankaya will be the property
of Kayı, from now onward.

572
01:01:31,986 --> 01:01:33,666
Thank Allah!

573
01:01:44,632 --> 01:01:47,132
I wouldn't want to give
you such bad news...

574
01:01:47,652 --> 01:01:51,372
...when you're in a pleasant state, but...

575
01:01:52,098 --> 01:01:54,748
...we just got word from Konya...

576
01:01:55,981 --> 01:01:58,381
...Osman has arrived at Konya...

577
01:01:58,785 --> 01:02:00,895
...and met with Sultan.

578
01:02:04,446 --> 01:02:06,266
Thank goodness!

579
01:02:07,231 --> 01:02:09,141
Thank you, Allah!

580
01:02:09,504 --> 01:02:12,194
He stabbed Sultan in the back.

581
01:02:15,916 --> 01:02:18,406
He tried to kill him.

582
01:02:19,752 --> 01:02:21,962
And then escaped.

583
01:02:22,784 --> 01:02:24,384
What?

584
01:02:27,947 --> 01:02:31,677
Your brother has no chance
to redeem himself anymore.

585
01:02:33,530 --> 01:02:36,330
If he ever falls into my hands...

586
01:02:36,773 --> 01:02:39,753
...don't you dare standing in my way.

587
01:02:41,172 --> 01:02:43,562
I will take his life the moment I see him.

588
01:02:49,397 --> 01:02:54,617
Your duty is to be a
worthy bey to your tribe.

589
01:02:55,432 --> 01:02:57,742
You have to qualify for being a bey.

590
01:03:10,172 --> 01:03:12,142
Osman...

591
01:03:13,192 --> 01:03:18,602
...find him and get him
to me alive and well.

592
01:03:21,661 --> 01:03:25,121
Sultan Mesut your excellence,
Osman tried to kill you.

593
01:03:25,245 --> 01:03:27,495
He killed commander Tebugay and escaped.

594
01:03:27,689 --> 01:03:30,479
We're looking for Osman, when
we find him we will kill him.

595
01:03:30,479 --> 01:03:32,499
Osman will not die!

596
01:03:37,349 --> 01:03:41,199
I will personally ask him...

597
01:03:41,973 --> 01:03:43,873
...the things he has done.

598
01:03:45,974 --> 01:03:47,644
Find him and get him here.

599
01:03:57,386 --> 01:03:59,356
Osman will die.

600
01:04:01,437 --> 01:04:05,567
And what's more is, he himself
will come to his own death.

601
01:04:07,491 --> 01:04:10,011
How is Selcan Hatun?

602
01:04:10,228 --> 01:04:11,948
Now well, my Vizier.

603
01:04:12,114 --> 01:04:13,834
Her wound is too deep.

604
01:04:17,161 --> 01:04:22,161
What will Osman do when her
mother is on her deathbed, Konur?

605
01:04:24,783 --> 01:04:28,133
Naturally, he'll go to visit his mother.

606
01:04:30,597 --> 01:04:33,387
Do not avert your eyes from the monastery.

607
01:04:35,841 --> 01:04:37,861
I'm at your command, my vizier.

608
01:04:50,601 --> 01:04:53,831
Dear Allah the greatest,...

609
01:04:57,778 --> 01:05:02,638
I'm never afraid of
the trap of the cruel...

610
01:05:04,890 --> 01:05:07,130
...or the mischief of the hypocrite.

611
01:05:08,970 --> 01:05:11,640
I always pray to you and...

612
01:05:12,958 --> 01:05:17,098
...always trust your plan.

613
01:05:19,009 --> 01:05:20,849
Dear Allah,...

614
01:05:23,750 --> 01:05:25,640
...dear Allah,...

615
01:05:26,645 --> 01:05:31,265
...allow me and my generation to spread...

616
01:05:32,334 --> 01:05:35,794
...the holy word to the entire world.

617
01:05:37,300 --> 01:05:40,450
Help me to stand still on the path...

618
01:05:41,009 --> 01:05:45,759
...of spreading your words, dear Allah!

619
01:05:53,689 --> 01:05:56,199
The merciful,...

620
01:05:57,280 --> 01:06:00,150
...the gracious Allah...

621
01:06:02,038 --> 01:06:06,888
...protect us from all the small or big...

622
01:06:07,744 --> 01:06:12,094
...misdeeds standing in the way of...

623
01:06:13,383 --> 01:06:15,993
...spreading Islam to the whole world.

624
01:06:24,816 --> 01:06:26,336
Dear Allah,...

625
01:06:28,902 --> 01:06:31,872
...If I'm in this trouble now, it's the...

626
01:06:33,222 --> 01:06:37,882
...the dream of this blessed government
that got me into this trouble.

627
01:06:41,766 --> 01:06:43,626
Dear Allah...

628
01:06:46,187 --> 01:06:49,127
...allow me to honorable redeem myself...

629
01:06:50,545 --> 01:06:53,345
...from all the smears thrown on me.

630
01:06:55,591 --> 01:06:59,341
Grace me with brothers of
the same objective, dear Allah!

631
01:07:00,406 --> 01:07:04,046
So that, I can spread your name,...

632
01:07:04,637 --> 01:07:08,637
...the belief of Islam to the whole world.

633
01:07:10,171 --> 01:07:12,191
Dear Allah,...

634
01:07:12,526 --> 01:07:17,906
...I got one life and I sacrifice it
for your path, dear Allah!

635
01:07:20,899 --> 01:07:25,709
You, you are the wisest.

636
01:07:31,711 --> 01:07:34,571
Give me strength to...

637
01:07:36,022 --> 01:07:38,732
...overcome these struggles.

638
01:07:40,459 --> 01:07:45,399
Give me strength to make this blessed...

639
01:07:46,045 --> 01:07:49,485
...government dominate the entire world.

640
01:07:51,968 --> 01:07:54,188
Amen, Dear Allah!

641
01:08:02,632 --> 01:08:03,792
Amen!

642
01:08:05,772 --> 01:08:08,592
How did you handle this, Bamsı Bey?

643
01:08:09,370 --> 01:08:12,050
You buried your brothers, like me.

644
01:08:30,180 --> 01:08:32,149
Give me advice,...

645
01:08:34,354 --> 01:08:36,644
...the dual weapons of Bamsı Bey.

646
01:08:40,879 --> 01:08:43,868
Bamsı Bey suffered all the pain I have.

647
01:08:44,697 --> 01:08:47,127
You witnessed all of it.

648
01:08:53,846 --> 01:08:56,647
How did he handle it?
Tell me!

649
01:09:03,680 --> 01:09:05,501
Tell me!

650
01:09:10,256 --> 01:09:12,707
Were you the ones that gave him strength?

651
01:09:14,318 --> 01:09:16,207
Give it to me as well!

652
01:09:22,606 --> 01:09:23,996
Tell me!

653
01:09:26,850 --> 01:09:29,770
What am I going to do, now?

654
01:09:50,624 --> 01:09:51,924
Tell me!

655
01:09:54,272 --> 01:09:55,552
Tell me!

656
01:09:57,586 --> 01:10:00,276
One of my brothers have gotten martyred.

657
01:10:01,347 --> 01:10:03,667
The other has lost his
mind more than I have.

658
01:10:04,714 --> 01:10:06,444
What am I going to do now?

659
01:10:07,103 --> 01:10:10,443
What am I supposed to do?
What am I supposed to do?

660
01:10:10,835 --> 01:10:12,915
What am I supposed to do?

661
01:10:19,069 --> 01:10:22,439
I am supposed to be virtuous...

662
01:10:23,183 --> 01:10:25,453
...just like Bamsı Bey.

663
01:10:26,431 --> 01:10:30,431
I am supposed to kill them
all with these weapons!

664
01:10:35,526 --> 01:10:36,886
I promise!

665
01:10:39,408 --> 01:10:41,198
I will butcher them all...

666
01:10:50,501 --> 01:10:52,591
...with these weapons!

667
01:10:56,551 --> 01:10:58,271
Brother!

668
01:11:02,359 --> 01:11:05,349
Now, I understand your reputation.

669
01:11:07,030 --> 01:11:09,610
We're in a terrible state...

670
01:11:10,871 --> 01:11:13,041
...and you vow to get revenge.

671
01:11:14,057 --> 01:11:16,237
You are out of your mind.

672
01:11:18,100 --> 01:11:20,520
It's not about using weapons, brother.

673
01:11:23,577 --> 01:11:25,697
It's about heart.

674
01:11:26,137 --> 01:11:29,157
It's about believing.

675
01:11:30,714 --> 01:11:31,934
It is not enough...

676
01:11:33,355 --> 01:11:35,935
...to lead men.

677
01:11:37,144 --> 01:11:39,054
You have to make them believe it.

678
01:11:40,607 --> 01:11:42,717
My bey made us believe it.

679
01:11:44,231 --> 01:11:47,871
My bey gave us courage.

680
01:11:51,349 --> 01:11:52,809
What about you?

681
01:11:53,203 --> 01:11:55,263
I came all the way from Caucaus.

682
01:11:56,245 --> 01:11:58,275
I followed Osman Bey.

683
01:11:59,156 --> 01:12:01,176
I am one of the believers, brother.

684
01:12:07,654 --> 01:12:09,934
If you lost a brother,...

685
01:12:10,205 --> 01:12:12,425
...you've gained one, know that.

686
01:12:23,770 --> 01:12:25,780
Praise be, my brothers!

687
01:12:26,100 --> 01:12:27,850
Praise be!

688
01:12:31,935 --> 01:12:33,115
İNEGÖL CASTLE

689
01:12:33,258 --> 01:12:34,258
Vizier Alam Shah!

690
01:12:37,902 --> 01:12:39,902
Vizier Alam Shah!

691
01:12:40,984 --> 01:12:43,734
I have important news, Nikola.

692
01:12:44,104 --> 01:12:47,194
When do you ever give unimportant news?

693
01:12:49,943 --> 01:12:54,923
We tricked Osman so well in Konya.

694
01:12:56,194 --> 01:13:00,874
He is now a traitor who
intended to kill Sultan Mesut.

695
01:13:04,987 --> 01:13:06,977
How did that happen?

696
01:13:07,555 --> 01:13:09,775
That is my secret.

697
01:13:12,597 --> 01:13:15,737
We now got Osman out of our way, forever?

698
01:13:18,495 --> 01:13:22,645
Right? Osman no longer has a head...

699
01:13:22,726 --> 01:13:24,436
...upon his body, right?

700
01:13:24,771 --> 01:13:26,341
Not yet.

701
01:13:27,206 --> 01:13:32,166
Osman somehow found a
way to escape from the palace.

702
01:13:34,181 --> 01:13:37,431
To hell with him! How could this happen?

703
01:13:37,601 --> 01:13:41,110
How could you let him slip away from your
hands when you managed to pin such a...

704
01:13:41,110 --> 01:13:42,170
...major crime on him?

705
01:13:42,170 --> 01:13:45,040
This is such a disappointment,
Vizier Alam Shah!

706
01:13:45,196 --> 01:13:51,076
Finding Kosses who we thought was in
Constantinople, helping Osman in Konya...

707
01:13:51,325 --> 01:13:54,105
...was a greater disappointment, Nikola.

708
01:13:56,990 --> 01:13:58,700
You tell me,...

709
01:13:59,154 --> 01:14:01,224
...what was he doing there?

710
01:14:01,607 --> 01:14:04,837
I should have killed Kosses
before he got to Constantinople!

711
01:14:04,939 --> 01:14:07,029
It is what it is, Nikola.

712
01:14:07,237 --> 01:14:10,127
No point in whining now.

713
01:14:10,608 --> 01:14:14,958
But you should not hide your failures...

714
01:14:15,725 --> 01:14:18,445
...like how you don't hide your victories.

715
01:14:19,079 --> 01:14:23,959
You don't hide them so that we know...

716
01:14:24,174 --> 01:14:26,744
...exactly what we're dealing with.

717
01:14:28,912 --> 01:14:34,032
And you do not need to
worry about Osman either...

718
01:14:34,032 --> 01:14:38,032
...Seljuk soldiers will
find him sooner or later.

719
01:14:39,196 --> 01:14:42,096
His head will not stay
on his body for long.

720
01:14:43,822 --> 01:14:47,182
Then, I promise that,...

721
01:14:48,668 --> 01:14:52,868
...I will find Kosses myself
and kill him with my hands.

722
01:14:53,583 --> 01:14:55,213
I promise!

723
01:14:56,064 --> 01:14:58,434
I trust you, Nikola.

724
01:14:58,882 --> 01:15:00,832
Do what you say.

725
01:15:03,917 --> 01:15:07,517
The samples of the goods that we will
bring to the bazaar will come here...

726
01:15:07,773 --> 01:15:11,753
...by tomorrow morning. I will personally
show them to you, by early in the morning.

727
01:15:12,434 --> 01:15:14,334
That's why...

728
01:15:15,770 --> 01:15:18,970
...tonight, I am a guest
at your castle, Nikola.

729
01:15:20,067 --> 01:15:22,277
I would be honored.

730
01:15:32,628 --> 01:15:34,588
Where is Osman?

731
01:15:36,559 --> 01:15:38,419
Where is Osman?

732
01:15:39,975 --> 01:15:41,975
Tell my Osman...

733
01:15:43,330 --> 01:15:46,000
...that your mother does
gives her blessings to you.

734
01:15:50,632 --> 01:15:54,632
Always be one on the path for Osman's...

735
01:15:57,964 --> 01:16:00,244
...dream for the government.

736
01:16:03,611 --> 01:16:06,961
If Allah permits, you will
see those days together.

737
01:16:07,073 --> 01:16:10,713
Don't say that, mother! If Allah
permits, we will all see it together.

738
01:16:11,313 --> 01:16:13,013
It's destiny my girl.

739
01:16:13,405 --> 01:16:16,625
I was destined to see him become a bey...

740
01:16:18,323 --> 01:16:21,663
...but I guess I am not destined to
see him form his own government.

741
01:16:23,992 --> 01:16:25,812
It all will happen, aunt.

742
01:16:26,217 --> 01:16:28,897
Those days will happen
as well if Allah permits.

743
01:16:29,306 --> 01:16:33,166
My Osman dreams about the sacred...

744
01:16:33,462 --> 01:16:35,282
...government, right?

745
01:16:36,354 --> 01:16:38,684
Know that your children...

746
01:16:38,874 --> 01:16:42,764
...will be the expression
of Osman's dream.

747
01:16:45,121 --> 01:16:49,121
It is your, the mothers' duty to teach...

748
01:16:49,726 --> 01:16:52,276
...that to your children.

749
01:16:52,675 --> 01:16:55,945
Mothers are the chasteners of the tent...

750
01:16:57,237 --> 01:16:59,577
...they are the rearers of it.

751
01:17:00,962 --> 01:17:02,922
From a family, a tribe grows,...

752
01:17:04,188 --> 01:17:07,148
...from a tribe, a government grows.

753
01:17:12,107 --> 01:17:16,997
The government that my Osman will
establish will be stronger with...

754
01:17:17,154 --> 01:17:19,984
...your merciful, noble hands.

755
01:17:23,916 --> 01:17:25,656
My Orhan...

756
01:17:26,741 --> 01:17:28,681
...and my Korhan...

757
01:17:29,400 --> 01:17:34,920
...will stand by their
brother, no matter what.

758
01:17:38,920 --> 01:17:43,580
I know that you will raise your
children to...

759
01:17:44,062 --> 01:17:46,932
...serve for their government.

760
01:17:57,348 --> 01:18:00,278
What is it that is
motherless in the universe?

761
01:18:00,278 --> 01:18:02,718
Let the government be motherless.

762
01:18:04,200 --> 01:18:06,270
Eventually,...

763
01:18:06,524 --> 01:18:09,284
...the government my
Osman will establish...

764
01:18:09,547 --> 01:18:13,877
...will become better with
you two valiant mothers.

765
01:18:20,315 --> 01:18:22,355
Thank Allah!

766
01:18:25,027 --> 01:18:27,477
I want everything to be perfect, Erdoğdu!

767
01:18:27,545 --> 01:18:28,785
Did you hear me?

768
01:18:30,332 --> 01:18:33,862
Seeing that infidel Nikola who hurt my
mother and my sisters...

769
01:18:34,375 --> 01:18:39,195
...sitting on the Harmankaya throne
makes me boil over.

770
01:18:41,078 --> 01:18:43,898
Harmankaya will belong to Kayı.

771
01:18:44,310 --> 01:18:46,330
Alps can't wait for conquest, my bey.

772
01:18:46,831 --> 01:18:48,691
We are ready.

773
01:18:49,216 --> 01:18:51,816
With Allah's permission,
we will conquer Harmankaya.

774
01:18:52,739 --> 01:18:54,369
That we will.

775
01:18:54,792 --> 01:18:56,432
We will.

776
01:18:56,913 --> 01:18:59,373
Come on, go be with your alps.

777
01:18:59,972 --> 01:19:01,712
Yes, my bey.

778
01:19:12,471 --> 01:19:14,341
Osman has gotten himself...

779
01:19:16,066 --> 01:19:18,206
...in a lot of trouble, Ayşe.

780
01:19:19,956 --> 01:19:22,446
They say that he tried to kill the Sultan.

781
01:19:27,173 --> 01:19:29,333
Fortunately, Sultan did not die.

782
01:19:31,035 --> 01:19:32,795
It's all slander, my bey.

783
01:19:33,386 --> 01:19:35,336
Osman Bey would
never do such a thing.

784
01:19:37,055 --> 01:19:39,855
Osman has done all kinds of things lately.

785
01:19:40,059 --> 01:19:41,859
All kinds of things.

786
01:19:42,531 --> 01:19:46,281
What they say even makes
me have a suspicion.

787
01:19:49,319 --> 01:19:53,319
He is the one who made everything worse...

788
01:19:53,399 --> 01:19:56,209
...by escaping and not surrendering
when he should have.

789
01:20:01,050 --> 01:20:03,070
Oh, my brother.

790
01:20:05,126 --> 01:20:07,666
I wish you had listened to me.

791
01:20:08,525 --> 01:20:10,115
Gündüz.

792
01:20:10,382 --> 01:20:12,642
They have tricked Osman Bey.

793
01:20:12,835 --> 01:20:16,265
Osman Bey would never draw
his weapon on Sultan Mesut.

794
01:20:19,035 --> 01:20:20,625
I don't know, Ayşe.

795
01:20:21,412 --> 01:20:22,792
I don't know.

796
01:20:22,988 --> 01:20:25,528
Nothing is clear.

797
01:20:25,747 --> 01:20:27,217
I don't know.

798
01:20:29,490 --> 01:20:30,720
However,...

799
01:20:33,880 --> 01:20:37,240
...nobody will know of this crime
that's been pinned on Osman.

800
01:20:37,373 --> 01:20:38,823
Don't you dare!

801
01:20:44,377 --> 01:20:48,917
If Seljuk does not impound our tribe
after everything, Osman has done...

802
01:20:49,820 --> 01:20:51,780
...it is because of Alam Shah.

803
01:20:54,082 --> 01:20:55,622
But,...

804
01:20:56,565 --> 01:21:00,915
...I will do whatever I can for our tribe.

805
01:21:02,485 --> 01:21:05,045
Kayı Tribe will be prosperous!

806
01:21:05,360 --> 01:21:08,750
Kayı Oba will be peaceful!

807
01:21:10,511 --> 01:21:15,691
To do that, I will make Harmankaya
belong to Kayı.

808
01:21:27,741 --> 01:21:28,857
Boran,

809
01:21:31,644 --> 01:21:33,934
Osman Bey has escaped alive.

810
01:21:36,081 --> 01:21:38,961
Thank you, Allah.

811
01:21:39,132 --> 01:21:40,652
Don't be so happy yet.

812
01:21:42,227 --> 01:21:44,947
Vizier is up to some treacherous games.

813
01:21:46,379 --> 01:21:49,399
He knows Osman Bey will visit Selcan
Hatun one way or another.

814
01:21:50,281 --> 01:21:52,501
He requests a title deed for the monastery

815
01:21:52,536 --> 01:21:55,086
That weasel!

816
01:21:55,674 --> 01:21:58,984
The pain he has caused the games
he has played weren't enough...

817
01:21:59,112 --> 01:22:00,732
...he is now up to more.

818
01:22:02,450 --> 01:22:04,220
We should inform Osman Bey of this.

819
01:22:04,220 --> 01:22:06,630
I'll do it. I'll do it.

820
01:22:07,364 --> 01:22:09,044
Where is my bey now?

821
01:22:09,432 --> 01:22:11,282
He is on his way here from Konya.

822
01:22:13,768 --> 01:22:15,358
May Allah bless you!

823
01:22:16,358 --> 01:22:18,728
The places we hide in
the forest are apparent.

824
01:22:19,281 --> 01:22:21,421
I know where to find my bey.

825
01:22:22,573 --> 01:22:24,063
Boran,...

826
01:22:24,611 --> 01:22:28,211
...don't tell anyone that
the news came from me.

827
01:22:30,023 --> 01:22:32,333
This is our secret.

828
01:22:37,415 --> 01:22:38,805
May Allah bless you!

829
01:23:05,803 --> 01:23:07,313
Amen!

830
01:23:20,722 --> 01:23:22,292
My valiant,...

831
01:23:23,899 --> 01:23:25,419
...Göktuğ.

832
01:23:29,717 --> 01:23:31,397
Brother.

833
01:23:33,479 --> 01:23:35,009
Brother!

834
01:23:38,515 --> 01:23:40,315
My martyr.

835
01:23:54,482 --> 01:23:57,472
Let Allah bring us together
again in heaven.

836
01:24:05,140 --> 01:24:07,370
I promise,...

837
01:24:08,737 --> 01:24:12,737
...that I will get vengeance for you
and for all of our martyrs.

838
01:24:14,401 --> 01:24:16,361
Brother,...

839
01:24:17,152 --> 01:24:21,732
...you believed Allah's
word with all your heart.

840
01:24:23,740 --> 01:24:26,150
My brave brother.

841
01:24:28,972 --> 01:24:31,322
We are content with you.

842
01:24:36,470 --> 01:24:39,380
Let Allah be content as well.

843
01:24:47,014 --> 01:24:48,554
Göktuğ,

844
01:24:50,077 --> 01:24:52,217
My brother.

845
01:24:55,947 --> 01:24:59,007
I guess it's my destiny
to fight without you.

846
01:25:02,387 --> 01:25:04,597
It will be difficult, Göktuğ.

847
01:25:09,267 --> 01:25:12,097
Your absence breaks my heart brother.

848
01:25:16,136 --> 01:25:18,856
We will get revenge for brother Göktuğ.

849
01:25:23,043 --> 01:25:24,803
Don't worry about it, brother.

850
01:25:32,562 --> 01:25:34,542
We will.

851
01:25:36,010 --> 01:25:37,600
We won't break.

852
01:25:39,477 --> 01:25:44,947
Göktuğ was the friend
we always wanted to have.

853
01:25:49,853 --> 01:25:51,873
We're here, Cerkutay.

854
01:25:52,885 --> 01:25:54,555
We're here.

855
01:26:07,959 --> 01:26:09,049
Turgut.

856
01:26:09,198 --> 01:26:10,588
Yes, OsmanBey.

857
01:26:10,635 --> 01:26:12,125
Kosses,

858
01:26:12,778 --> 01:26:15,198
Go to Yirce with alps.

859
01:26:15,837 --> 01:26:17,647
We'll meet there.

860
01:26:18,540 --> 01:26:21,420
We'll go but what about you?

861
01:26:21,720 --> 01:26:23,877
It's very dangerous, Osman Bey.

862
01:26:24,150 --> 01:26:26,020
They're looking for you everywhere.

863
01:26:27,153 --> 01:26:29,753
My way is to salvation.

864
01:26:30,900 --> 01:26:32,990
Do not worry.

865
01:26:33,757 --> 01:26:35,417
May Allah bless you!

866
01:26:57,829 --> 01:27:00,909
You've never seen anything
like it in this soil, Nikola.

867
01:27:03,593 --> 01:27:05,753
I really haven't

868
01:27:05,825 --> 01:27:07,255
Very sharp.

869
01:27:08,301 --> 01:27:11,601
We'll earn a lot in this bazaar.

870
01:27:13,833 --> 01:27:17,293
But, these are the most important.

871
01:27:34,390 --> 01:27:36,380
HARMANKAYA CASTLE

872
01:28:00,411 --> 01:28:02,791
Why did you throng here
with a crowd, Gündüz Bey?

873
01:28:03,056 --> 01:28:04,926
Is there something we do not know?

874
01:28:05,501 --> 01:28:07,411
We did not come for a visit.

875
01:28:08,417 --> 01:28:10,727
We're here to take the castle.

876
01:28:11,105 --> 01:28:12,695
Soldiers!

877
01:28:28,590 --> 01:28:31,620
Do you think I don't know
of your cunningness?

878
01:28:34,600 --> 01:28:37,170
So, Nikola gathered
the castle with soldiers?

879
01:28:38,261 --> 01:28:40,231
Come on, Valiants!

880
01:29:12,307 --> 01:29:15,267
Come on, Valiants! Show no mercy!

881
01:29:33,849 --> 01:29:35,589
Salam aleikum!

882
01:29:35,881 --> 01:29:39,471
Aleikum salam!

883
01:29:47,681 --> 01:29:50,751
We heard that Geyhatu has come back.

884
01:29:53,618 --> 01:29:55,088
His goal is to...

885
01:29:56,933 --> 01:29:59,153
...cost Argun Khan the throne.

886
01:30:00,548 --> 01:30:05,408
He wants to have power in this soil.

887
01:30:07,161 --> 01:30:08,771
That's true.

888
01:30:08,931 --> 01:30:11,601
He is in preparation for a
rebellion against Argun Khan

889
01:30:11,745 --> 01:30:14,465
He aims to conquer the entire land...

890
01:30:14,482 --> 01:30:17,002
...and create a gigantic army.

891
01:30:17,567 --> 01:30:22,527
Lords, Turkmen Beys, he'll
take them all along with him.

892
01:30:22,622 --> 01:30:25,982
Vizier Alam Shah is working with him.

893
01:30:26,024 --> 01:30:28,594
He wants to control Seljuk.

894
01:30:28,787 --> 01:30:31,647
That way he'll grow his army even bigger.

895
01:30:32,694 --> 01:30:36,694
Unless you prevent that from
happening of course.

896
01:30:37,762 --> 01:30:40,292
The breath I take is for that.

897
01:30:41,344 --> 01:30:43,794
That is the only thing
that beats my heart.

898
01:30:44,484 --> 01:30:47,214
It is the dream of a government
that keeps me standing.

899
01:30:50,473 --> 01:30:52,423
Tell us then,...

900
01:30:52,872 --> 01:30:54,602
...what are you going to do now?

901
01:30:55,510 --> 01:30:57,530
Politics.

902
01:30:59,469 --> 01:31:02,089
If they want to play a game...

903
01:31:03,735 --> 01:31:08,315
...if they want to break the rules...

904
01:31:10,515 --> 01:31:14,515
...if they try to set up an order
that we say is detrimental...

905
01:31:16,066 --> 01:31:20,206
...then, I will destroy them.

906
01:31:23,613 --> 01:31:25,943
Vizier Alam Shah...

907
01:31:27,498 --> 01:31:29,738
...created a unit.

908
01:31:30,769 --> 01:31:32,529
I will destroy it.

909
01:31:35,509 --> 01:31:38,129
If the goal of Geyhatu and
Vizier Alam Shah is to...

910
01:31:38,676 --> 01:31:42,876
...take down the Lords and gain power...

911
01:31:44,822 --> 01:31:47,182
...I will prevent that from happening.

912
01:31:47,602 --> 01:31:50,112
You said well, but...

913
01:31:50,403 --> 01:31:53,073
...tell us how you're going
to do that Osman Bey.

914
01:31:53,279 --> 01:31:54,959
Lord Kosses,...

915
01:31:56,382 --> 01:31:58,672
...has been with me for a while.

916
01:31:59,022 --> 01:32:03,142
Now I'm going to get the weakest link...

917
01:32:03,836 --> 01:32:05,956
...on my side.

918
01:32:08,291 --> 01:32:12,241
İnegöl Lord, Aya Nikola.

919
01:32:16,744 --> 01:32:21,034
If my brother and my beys
turn their backs on me...

920
01:32:21,605 --> 01:32:25,105
...then, I'll confront them...

921
01:32:26,740 --> 01:32:29,320
...with soldiers of lords.

922
01:32:30,280 --> 01:32:33,830
I will not leave these
lands, these soils...

923
01:32:34,616 --> 01:32:39,626
...to Geyhatu's and Vizier Alam Shah's
treacherous ambitions.

924
01:32:40,481 --> 01:32:42,481
Never.

925
01:32:42,917 --> 01:32:45,997
Alam Shah, Gündüz Bey have
started to move already.

926
01:32:46,655 --> 01:32:48,605
They have gone to take Harmankaya.

927
01:32:49,925 --> 01:32:51,555
Whereas you are in front of us.

928
01:32:52,898 --> 01:32:54,878
You're too late, Osman Bey.

929
01:32:57,982 --> 01:32:59,962
I know, may Allah bless you!

930
01:33:00,311 --> 01:33:02,751
Vizier Alam Shah's aim is not to...

931
01:33:03,356 --> 01:33:06,036
...strenghten the lords.

932
01:33:06,901 --> 01:33:09,071
It is to destroy them.

933
01:33:09,886 --> 01:33:13,606
That's why I had informed Nikola before.

934
01:33:14,514 --> 01:33:16,654
He probably took precautions.

935
01:33:18,540 --> 01:33:22,300
Do you have faith that Nikola
can stop this, Osman Bey?

936
01:33:23,937 --> 01:33:25,077
Never.

937
01:33:28,324 --> 01:33:29,164
But,...

938
01:33:32,003 --> 01:33:34,333
...I have decided who to side with...

939
01:33:35,241 --> 01:33:38,101
...when I'm on the edges.

940
01:33:38,910 --> 01:33:41,010
I showed him the way.

941
01:33:42,107 --> 01:33:44,247
He'll be with us too.

942
01:33:44,480 --> 01:33:49,660
Until the government, we
planted the seeds for...

943
01:33:50,371 --> 01:33:52,391
...is established.

944
01:33:53,187 --> 01:33:58,507
Then, all the tyrants will pay.

945
01:33:59,905 --> 01:34:01,515
Ertuğrul Bey.

946
01:34:03,204 --> 01:34:05,174
May he rest in peace.

947
01:34:05,174 --> 01:34:06,934
Amen.

948
01:34:07,642 --> 01:34:11,452
He was right to make you a bey.

949
01:34:13,064 --> 01:34:15,174
Let's get to the main point.

950
01:34:16,266 --> 01:34:18,416
Turkmen tribes are revolting.

951
01:34:19,702 --> 01:34:23,702
To ease the rebellion,
Argun Khan is sending...

952
01:34:23,779 --> 01:34:27,939
...an army of twenty thousand
men to Geyhatun's commands.

953
01:34:30,410 --> 01:34:33,540
He'll be even more powerful with them.

954
01:34:35,025 --> 01:34:36,855
Rebellion is an excuse.

955
01:34:38,622 --> 01:34:40,822
These edges are not his concern.

956
01:34:43,312 --> 01:34:45,722
The entire land is.

957
01:34:47,346 --> 01:34:49,436
Hurry up, Osman Bey.

958
01:34:50,291 --> 01:34:53,851
On the verge of handling one trouble
the other is on the way.

959
01:34:54,468 --> 01:34:57,298
The destiny of the Turk is in your hand.

960
01:35:05,368 --> 01:35:07,288
May Allah bless you, Osman Bey!

961
01:35:10,494 --> 01:35:13,484
We have no doubt, but we'd like to know...

962
01:35:13,593 --> 01:35:15,403
...where are you heading, Osman Bey?

963
01:35:22,890 --> 01:35:25,000
To Kızıl Elma.

964
01:35:28,368 --> 01:35:33,178
No power, no struggle
can stand in our way.

965
01:35:35,698 --> 01:35:37,578
We're not alone on this path.

966
01:35:38,858 --> 01:35:41,328
Even if we're not in our tribe...

967
01:35:42,048 --> 01:35:45,008
...our tribe works like a sharp weapon...

968
01:35:45,977 --> 01:35:48,357
...you beat it in heat.

969
01:35:51,673 --> 01:35:53,823
Godspeed!

970
01:35:53,933 --> 01:35:55,883
May I Allah bless you, Osman Bey!

971
01:35:55,990 --> 01:35:58,510
May Allah help you!

972
01:36:15,726 --> 01:36:18,016
- Allah is eternal!
- Allah is right!

973
01:36:18,560 --> 01:36:19,900
Allah is eternal!

974
01:36:28,719 --> 01:36:31,559
Our bey wants it, we do it!

975
01:36:31,729 --> 01:36:35,889
He goes through all kinds of trouble
and still has a lust for conquest.

976
01:36:36,600 --> 01:36:39,440
You have come here
believing as well brothers!

977
01:36:39,440 --> 01:36:43,990
These weapons will not
enter the holsters of alps dry.

978
01:36:44,488 --> 01:36:46,908
They'll be soaked with
the blood of tyrants.

979
01:36:46,959 --> 01:36:49,479
- We believe it!
- We believe it!

980
01:36:50,138 --> 01:36:53,468
We beat weapons today,...

981
01:36:53,684 --> 01:36:56,594
...walls tomorrow.

982
01:36:56,769 --> 01:36:59,189
If Allah permits, conquest is near.

983
01:36:59,235 --> 01:37:01,095
- If Allah permits!
- If Allah permits!

984
01:37:01,095 --> 01:37:03,415
Allah is the greatest!

985
01:37:03,448 --> 01:37:05,938
Allah is the greatest!

986
01:37:06,027 --> 01:37:09,007
Allah is the greatest!

987
01:37:09,229 --> 01:37:11,959
Allah is the greatest!

988
01:37:12,174 --> 01:37:13,544
Allah is the greatest!

989
01:37:24,964 --> 01:37:30,044
Sir, Gündüz Bey, and his men have
attacked the Castle of Harmankaya.

990
01:37:30,112 --> 01:37:32,372
There were a lot of them.

991
01:37:32,540 --> 01:37:34,520
We have lost the castle, sir.

992
01:37:38,105 --> 01:37:40,655
Incompetents! Fools!

993
01:37:44,399 --> 01:37:46,249
Arguz!

994
01:37:48,591 --> 01:37:54,130
Every time I asked you, you sad
" The castle is safe sir"...

995
01:37:54,130 --> 01:37:58,010
...the castle you call safe
is now in the hands of Kayı!

996
01:38:07,106 --> 01:38:09,996
Don't act hotheaded, Nikola.

997
01:38:11,558 --> 01:38:14,118
You distracted me!

998
01:38:19,039 --> 01:38:24,259
You gave my castle to Gündüz
by distracting me, Vizier!

999
01:38:24,881 --> 01:38:26,641
Isn't that right?

1000
01:38:29,100 --> 01:38:32,120
You made a mistake, a very big mistake!

1001
01:38:32,843 --> 01:38:34,533
A very big mistake!

1002
01:38:35,355 --> 01:38:38,365
Mongols!
Geyhatu is approaching!

1003
01:38:50,219 --> 01:38:52,059
Open the gate!

1004
01:40:04,871 --> 01:40:09,371
Thank Allah, Harmankaya
now belongs to Kayı!

1005
01:40:09,888 --> 01:40:12,048
- Thank Allah!
- Thank Allah!

1006
01:40:12,885 --> 01:40:17,155
Thank Allah for gracing
us with this conquest!

1007
01:40:17,228 --> 01:40:19,338
- Thank Allah!
- Thank Allah!

1008
01:40:20,708 --> 01:40:26,158
I have to say that Vizier Alam Shah has
been very contributary for this conquest.

1009
01:40:27,718 --> 01:40:30,049
He wanted the best for the...

1010
01:40:30,049 --> 01:40:33,999
...Turkmen Tribes and the Kayı Tribe...

1011
01:40:34,883 --> 01:40:37,403
...and conduced with this conquest.

1012
01:40:39,903 --> 01:40:43,773
Vizier and I have the same goal in mind.

1013
01:40:46,151 --> 01:40:50,840
We want Turkmens to live
prosperously in the entire world.

1014
01:40:50,840 --> 01:40:52,710
- Amen!
- Amen!

1015
01:40:54,382 --> 01:40:58,382
On this mission, we won't shy away from...

1016
01:40:59,105 --> 01:41:03,785
...drawing our weapons or endangering
our own lives so help us, Allah!

1017
01:41:04,573 --> 01:41:07,373
May Allah bless your conquest, Gündüz Bey!

1018
01:41:08,615 --> 01:41:11,985
I was against you being a bey but,
you have surprised me...

1019
01:41:11,985 --> 01:41:14,935
...and it's a good thing
you did, Gündüz Bey.

1020
01:41:15,051 --> 01:41:17,871
- May you live long!
- May you live long!

1021
01:41:18,414 --> 01:41:21,744
May Allah bless you! All of
you may live long as well!

1022
01:41:22,948 --> 01:41:24,758
Do not forget,...

1023
01:41:25,329 --> 01:41:27,849
...once we're all together...

1024
01:41:28,069 --> 01:41:30,879
...these types of conquests will not stop!

1025
01:41:30,926 --> 01:41:34,146
- Thank Allah!
- Thank Allah!

1026
01:41:51,519 --> 01:41:52,919
Erdoğdu,...

1027
01:41:53,800 --> 01:41:56,070
...hand out the loots equally.

1028
01:41:56,070 --> 01:41:57,480
Yes, my bey!

1029
01:42:16,225 --> 01:42:17,975
May Allah bless you, my bey!

1030
01:42:20,488 --> 01:42:22,110
Thank you, Gündüz Bey!

1031
01:42:22,110 --> 01:42:24,330
Thank you, my bey!

1032
01:42:24,438 --> 01:42:25,838
Thank you, Gündüz Bey!

1033
01:42:25,902 --> 01:42:28,142
May Allah bless you, my bey!

1034
01:42:31,274 --> 01:42:34,314
Why don't we kill you, Nikola?

1035
01:42:34,733 --> 01:42:38,453
Why don't you kill me, Geyhatu?

1036
01:42:39,703 --> 01:42:45,213
Because you're a man whose shadow
is bigger than himself.

1037
01:42:47,179 --> 01:42:50,379
We need your shadow.

1038
01:42:52,376 --> 01:42:56,716
There is a Mongolian army
in your yard, Nikola.

1039
01:42:58,986 --> 01:43:01,846
Thanks to you, Vizier Alam Shah!

1040
01:43:02,637 --> 01:43:04,137
Thanks to you!

1041
01:43:04,137 --> 01:43:06,847
You don't have your lord
friends to help you neither.

1042
01:43:07,063 --> 01:43:09,283
We sent them packing, together.

1043
01:43:09,512 --> 01:43:12,332
Don't be blind like Osman.

1044
01:43:12,765 --> 01:43:16,275
Don't be blind so that
you won't live the same fate.

1045
01:43:18,294 --> 01:43:21,084
You're a wise man, Nikola.

1046
01:43:21,362 --> 01:43:22,902
Harmankaya,...

1047
01:43:23,981 --> 01:43:27,981
...is just a part of one
of our grand desires.

1048
01:43:28,937 --> 01:43:31,697
What are your grand desires?

1049
01:43:31,714 --> 01:43:35,714
Calm your nerves, Nikola!

1050
01:43:36,473 --> 01:43:42,493
Or I'll build a castle made of
y our and your soldiers' skulls.

1051
01:43:45,881 --> 01:43:49,881
Kayı Tribe now belongs to us.

1052
01:43:50,115 --> 01:43:52,905
Gündüz is in the palm of our hands, now.

1053
01:43:53,478 --> 01:43:56,448
Be sure that, that tribe is more
valuable than the castle.

1054
01:43:58,483 --> 01:44:03,653
Alright, but what do you
want from me and my castle?

1055
01:44:04,430 --> 01:44:07,530
Our enemies are the same.

1056
01:44:08,626 --> 01:44:11,546
The prize will be the same as well.

1057
01:44:12,875 --> 01:44:16,345
Kayı is ours.

1058
01:44:17,658 --> 01:44:20,608
Seljuk will be ours as well!

1059
01:44:22,849 --> 01:44:26,769
And you will form a government here.

1060
01:44:29,665 --> 01:44:33,665
Osman is a living dead...

1061
01:44:33,692 --> 01:44:35,722
...lords are banished.

1062
01:44:37,381 --> 01:44:40,091
Nobody is standing our way.

1063
01:44:40,829 --> 01:44:44,829
Harmankaya is just a little price we paid.

1064
01:44:47,898 --> 01:44:51,898
I'm going to make you a government, here.

1065
01:44:54,498 --> 01:44:58,048
I overthrow and build governments.

1066
01:45:02,059 --> 01:45:05,379
What is your offer, Geyhatu?

1067
01:45:06,160 --> 01:45:08,180
Don't you want to resurrect the...

1068
01:45:08,180 --> 01:45:12,560
...holy Roman Empire
on these lands, Nikola?

1069
01:45:14,164 --> 01:45:15,844
I would love to.

1070
01:45:16,289 --> 01:45:18,089
I would love to.

1071
01:45:18,872 --> 01:45:22,602
If you serve our interests
and be loyal to us...

1072
01:45:23,460 --> 01:45:26,930
...Geyhatu will make all
of that happen for you.

1073
01:45:28,520 --> 01:45:32,020
But Osman has to die as soon as possible.

1074
01:45:33,967 --> 01:45:38,377
He'll go to visit his mother Selcan Hatun.

1075
01:45:39,187 --> 01:45:40,737
Once Osman dies...

1076
01:45:42,062 --> 01:45:45,332
...we'll talk about the rest later.

1077
01:45:53,817 --> 01:45:55,717
Soldiers!

1078
01:46:14,579 --> 01:46:16,519
Mother Selcan,...

1079
01:46:18,601 --> 01:46:21,031
...Kayı's valiant mother...

1080
01:46:22,873 --> 01:46:26,503
...I will make them pay for what
they have done to her!

1081
01:46:28,073 --> 01:46:30,313
We will, brother.

1082
01:46:30,486 --> 01:46:32,646
We will if Allah permits.

1083
01:46:37,367 --> 01:46:41,807
May Allah help us to get revenge
on the tyrants for the oppressed.

1084
01:46:42,391 --> 01:46:43,711
Amen!

1085
01:46:46,272 --> 01:46:49,812
No crime will be without
punishment, Turgut.

1086
01:46:50,421 --> 01:46:53,824
I swear, whoever caused
all this suffering...

1087
01:46:53,824 --> 01:46:56,314
...will suffer themselves.

1088
01:46:57,582 --> 01:46:59,332
May Allah bless you, Kosses!

1089
01:47:01,477 --> 01:47:04,507
Brother, my bey is coming.

1090
01:47:16,407 --> 01:47:18,357
- Boran,
- My bey,

1091
01:47:19,055 --> 01:47:20,545
Brother,

1092
01:47:27,549 --> 01:47:29,239
Brother.

1093
01:47:30,272 --> 01:47:31,522
My bey.

1094
01:47:35,084 --> 01:47:37,084
I've got important news, my bey.

1095
01:47:37,168 --> 01:47:38,908
Tell me about it.

1096
01:47:43,332 --> 01:47:45,102
My bey, Gündüz Bey...

1097
01:47:47,667 --> 01:47:49,607
What is up with Gündüz Bey?

1098
01:47:50,018 --> 01:47:54,018
He banished the hatuns alongside with...

1099
01:47:54,485 --> 01:47:58,325
...the blacksmith from the tribe.

1100
01:48:14,422 --> 01:48:15,932
Brother.

1101
01:48:18,085 --> 01:48:19,745
Brother.

1102
01:48:20,673 --> 01:48:22,293
Brother!

1103
01:48:34,496 --> 01:48:36,216
My bey,

1104
01:48:37,105 --> 01:48:39,145
They got ambushed on the way.

1105
01:48:42,081 --> 01:48:43,651
What?

1106
01:48:45,451 --> 01:48:47,191
What are you saying?

1107
01:48:47,832 --> 01:48:49,692
What are you saying, Boran?

1108
01:48:49,692 --> 01:48:53,242
Orhan, my mother, Malhun
Bala, how are they?

1109
01:48:53,471 --> 01:48:55,111
Tell me!

1110
01:48:55,111 --> 01:48:57,241
Orhan is at the tribe, my bey.

1111
01:48:57,479 --> 01:48:59,029
Hatuns are well too.

1112
01:49:02,668 --> 01:49:04,838
However, Selcan Mother...

1113
01:49:07,476 --> 01:49:08,906
Mother.

1114
01:49:10,139 --> 01:49:16,519
My Bey, traitor vizier attacked the
Hatuns.

1115
01:49:16,973 --> 01:49:19,403
Selcan Mother is hurt.

1116
01:49:19,491 --> 01:49:23,491
She's in the lodge now.
Kumral Abdal is with her.

1117
01:49:24,901 --> 01:49:28,641
Mother... Is she okay?

1118
01:49:28,910 --> 01:49:32,120
Is she alive? Tell me.

1119
01:49:32,402 --> 01:49:34,422
I don't hide things from you, my Bey.

1120
01:49:35,315 --> 01:49:37,835
She is alive.

1121
01:49:37,866 --> 01:49:41,866
However, her wound...

1122
01:49:42,641 --> 01:49:45,171
is deep, my Bey.

1123
01:49:57,194 --> 01:50:01,394
Vizier... Vizier Alemşah...

1124
01:50:03,021 --> 01:50:06,041
Find a grave for yourself.

1125
01:50:06,211 --> 01:50:10,041
- Come on! Let's go to mother.
- Stop, my Bey.

1126
01:50:11,074 --> 01:50:14,104
Vizier knows you're going to the lodge.

1127
01:50:15,019 --> 01:50:18,219
He's ready.

1128
01:50:19,397 --> 01:50:23,397
If you go to the lodge,
you'll fall into his trap.

1129
01:50:27,488 --> 01:50:31,868
I won't let Vizier and his men harm us.

1130
01:50:34,306 --> 01:50:35,656
Boran.

1131
01:50:35,686 --> 01:50:39,686
We will go to my mother's.
Go to Edebalı.

1132
01:50:40,120 --> 01:50:42,690
He should tell all dervishes around.

1133
01:50:43,257 --> 01:50:47,257
He should invite them to Söğüt.

1134
01:50:47,324 --> 01:50:52,694
And we will go to Selcan Mother to Söğüt.

1135
01:50:52,952 --> 01:50:55,742
Your command, my Bey.

1136
01:51:06,953 --> 01:51:08,193
Come on.

1137
01:51:21,944 --> 01:51:25,944
It's because of me.

1138
01:51:26,100 --> 01:51:30,300
Don't say that, I saved my child.

1139
01:51:38,636 --> 01:51:40,926
I saved my children.

1140
01:51:46,337 --> 01:51:50,337
She has fever.
I should tell Kumral Abdal.

1141
01:51:50,398 --> 01:51:53,858
Come on, Zehra.

1142
01:51:57,133 --> 01:51:58,393
Mother.

1143
01:51:59,685 --> 01:52:02,575
No.

1144
01:52:10,255 --> 01:52:15,945
Mother. You're leaving me.

1145
01:52:17,021 --> 01:52:18,951
Don't.

1146
01:52:22,464 --> 01:52:28,224
Mother! No! Mother!

1147
01:52:28,894 --> 01:52:35,994
Mother! Mother!

1148
01:52:38,125 --> 01:52:42,765
Mother! Selcan Mother!

1149
01:52:51,546 --> 01:52:54,926
Welcome.

1150
01:52:55,219 --> 01:52:57,479
We've been waiting for you.

1151
01:52:57,758 --> 01:53:00,538
Thank Allah you're here.

1152
01:53:01,390 --> 01:53:05,000
My Sheikh will be happy to see you.

1153
01:53:23,957 --> 01:53:26,657
Watch them. I'll let Vizier know.

1154
01:53:26,701 --> 01:53:28,701
Your command.

1155
01:53:29,805 --> 01:53:33,315
We placed our soldiers everywhere, sir.

1156
01:53:33,401 --> 01:53:36,941
However, no one saw Osman.

1157
01:53:37,098 --> 01:53:40,038
He won't come, obviously.

1158
01:53:45,014 --> 01:53:48,034
Osman will come, Ferman.

1159
01:53:50,218 --> 01:53:56,078
He will want to see her
before his Selcan Mother dies.

1160
01:53:58,309 --> 01:54:00,409
Watch them carefully.

1161
01:54:00,682 --> 01:54:02,392
I don't want any mistakes.

1162
01:54:02,553 --> 01:54:06,793
- Can I come in, my Vizier?
- Come in.

1163
01:54:12,438 --> 01:54:15,918
Some people dressed as dervishes came.

1164
01:54:16,110 --> 01:54:20,780
They're in the lodge. Obviously, they
are Osman and his Alps.

1165
01:54:24,071 --> 01:54:28,071
Osman won't come
out of Söğüt today.

1166
01:54:28,331 --> 01:54:31,181
Söğüt will be his grave.

1167
01:54:35,375 --> 01:54:41,555
Come on let's visit Edebalı.

1168
01:55:26,089 --> 01:55:30,919
Look everywhere! Find Osman!

1169
01:55:31,034 --> 01:55:34,094
Look everywhere!

1170
01:55:41,630 --> 01:55:47,410
"And they argue with Us—forgetting
they were created—

1171
01:55:47,724 --> 01:55:55,034
...saying, “Who will give life to
decayed bones?...

1172
01:55:56,463 --> 01:56:06,273
...Say, ˹O Prophet,˺ “They will be revived by the One Who produced them the first time...

1173
01:56:07,861 --> 01:56:14,141
He has ˹perfect˺ knowledge of every
created being." -Surah Ya-Sin

1174
01:56:14,432 --> 01:56:17,272
Where's Osman, Edebalı?

1175
01:56:17,299 --> 01:56:18,819
Where did you hide him?

1176
01:56:18,962 --> 01:56:22,962
"Allah Almighty speaks the truth."

1177
01:56:23,230 --> 01:56:26,400
Show some respect!

1178
01:56:26,564 --> 01:56:31,204
You can't show up to a funeral like that!

1179
01:56:32,698 --> 01:56:36,868
Stop, Vizier Alemşah!

1180
01:56:43,423 --> 01:56:47,973
Find traitor Osman.
Look everywhere!

1181
01:56:48,204 --> 01:56:51,994
Even if he's lost, find him.

1182
01:56:53,974 --> 01:56:57,784
- Stop!
- Get out of my way, dervish.

1183
01:57:05,707 --> 01:57:11,947
You have no mercy to alive, don't you
have respect for the dead?

1184
01:57:12,767 --> 01:57:15,327
It's inconsiderate of you to do that.

1185
01:57:15,370 --> 01:57:20,000
It's inconsiderate of you to
help a traitor and hide him.

1186
01:57:32,487 --> 01:57:35,717
Where are you going?

1187
01:57:54,862 --> 01:57:58,552
Osman is here. I know.

1188
01:57:58,587 --> 01:58:02,457
What are you saying? We
have a dead! Don't you see?

1189
01:58:02,615 --> 01:58:05,445
We'll search the room.
Do it!

1190
01:58:05,629 --> 01:58:08,629
What are you doing? Don't you see
that we have a funeral?

1191
01:58:08,714 --> 01:58:12,714
It's a woman.
You can't come in here.

1192
01:58:18,314 --> 01:58:21,684
Get out.

1193
01:58:22,779 --> 01:58:26,779
You too, Celali. Don't you hear them?

1194
01:58:26,860 --> 01:58:28,940
Don't you have respect for the dead?

1195
01:58:29,189 --> 01:58:32,709
Konur, choose your side.

1196
01:58:32,805 --> 01:58:35,315
You are being too much.

1197
01:58:35,752 --> 01:58:39,622
You are being disrespectful.
I side with the right ones.

1198
01:58:40,680 --> 01:58:43,490
Stop what you're doing or I kill you.

1199
01:58:43,949 --> 01:58:48,959
I pretend to not hear that.
Let the soldiers do their job.

1200
01:58:49,661 --> 01:58:51,961
Osman is a traitor.

1201
01:58:52,583 --> 01:58:54,613
Search the room.

1202
01:58:56,398 --> 01:59:00,398
Don't you have a heart?

1203
01:59:03,647 --> 01:59:08,187
Forgive us.
Sorry for your loss.

1204
01:59:08,560 --> 01:59:10,370
Thank you.

1205
01:59:16,587 --> 01:59:18,787
Bring them.

1206
01:59:25,208 --> 01:59:30,408
Ever since you came, you've
been slandering people.

1207
01:59:31,473 --> 01:59:34,613
You are being very cruel...

1208
01:59:34,899 --> 01:59:38,689
and our Allah won't forgive that.

1209
01:59:40,255 --> 01:59:46,155
You're leading yourself to
hell because of that.

1210
01:59:46,355 --> 01:59:50,535
Stop talking about hell when
you are protecting a traitor.

1211
01:59:50,631 --> 01:59:55,381
You are the one who are going to hell.

1212
01:59:58,550 --> 02:00:03,670
You come here without respect and talk.

1213
02:00:04,595 --> 02:00:08,195
You are being disrespectful, you
don't know what pain is.

1214
02:00:08,950 --> 02:00:14,170
However, I see that dead people
are more alive than you.

1215
02:00:14,854 --> 02:00:17,704
They are less decayed.

1216
02:00:19,828 --> 02:00:23,828
Your soul is decayed and you don't
know that.

1217
02:00:24,643 --> 02:00:29,313
I will cut your tongues and cut
Osman's head.

1218
02:00:29,829 --> 02:00:32,649
Don't worry.

1219
02:00:34,067 --> 02:00:37,827
You'll see what decaying is then.

1220
02:00:39,484 --> 02:00:41,994
Bring them.

1221
02:00:49,715 --> 02:00:52,235
Open their faces.

1222
02:01:06,573 --> 02:01:08,913
Vizier Alemşah...

1223
02:01:12,099 --> 02:01:16,259
Whoever has evil in their hearts...

1224
02:01:17,330 --> 02:01:19,910
will be punished afterlife.

1225
02:01:20,220 --> 02:01:23,310
You will too.

1226
02:01:24,130 --> 02:01:28,800
My Allah won't always punish
people afterlife, may punish you alive.

1227
02:01:29,968 --> 02:01:34,128
You will be punished by valiants.

1228
02:01:36,411 --> 02:01:40,051
Your punishment will be
hard for you, Vizier Alemşah.

1229
02:01:45,348 --> 02:01:48,298
Ensheathe the swords.

1230
02:02:00,284 --> 02:02:03,564
Their punishments will be big...

1231
02:02:04,987 --> 02:02:08,107
when the time comes.

1232
02:02:44,611 --> 02:02:45,781
Oh.

1233
02:02:46,747 --> 02:02:53,287
I thought that only our cities and castles
are full of bridges and secret passages.

1234
02:02:56,178 --> 02:02:57,578
My Bey.

1235
02:02:58,393 --> 02:03:01,843
Under the Söğüt is dangerous.

1236
02:03:03,347 --> 02:03:06,967
We don't know what we need
and when we need.

1237
02:03:07,167 --> 02:03:11,167
This leads us to Vizier's death.

1238
02:03:14,279 --> 02:03:17,529
Alps. Listen to me carefully.

1239
02:03:17,700 --> 02:03:24,730
Kosses, catch the soldiers
you see and hide yourselves.

1240
02:03:28,632 --> 02:03:32,792
This night will become
Vizier's last night.

1241
02:03:35,722 --> 02:03:39,812
However, don't kill anyone
else except for him.

1242
02:03:42,061 --> 02:03:44,981
- Understand?
- Yes.

1243
02:03:45,381 --> 02:03:46,781
Come on.

1244
02:03:57,633 --> 02:03:58,713
Come on.

1245
02:04:48,600 --> 02:04:51,840
Come, Vizier Alemşah.

1246
02:04:52,478 --> 02:04:53,778
Come and...

1247
02:04:56,482 --> 02:04:58,882
let justice be done!

1248
02:05:09,648 --> 02:05:13,258
When he hears that my mother is dead...

1249
02:05:14,708 --> 02:05:17,588
he'll think that I will go to the funeral.

1250
02:05:17,969 --> 02:05:19,529
Mother.

1251
02:05:33,234 --> 02:05:35,954
My Osman. You came.

1252
02:05:36,113 --> 02:05:38,483
- I did, mother.
- Thank Allah.

1253
02:05:38,704 --> 02:05:43,414
- I came, mother.
- Thank Allah.

1254
02:05:47,644 --> 02:05:51,374
Kumra Abdal, how's she?

1255
02:05:51,508 --> 02:05:55,868
Thank Allah, she's fine. Her wound is...

1256
02:05:55,907 --> 02:05:59,907
not bad. She needs to rest.

1257
02:06:00,338 --> 02:06:02,748
My mother is a powerful Hatun.

1258
02:06:03,346 --> 02:06:06,016
She will be better.

1259
02:06:12,206 --> 02:06:13,626
She will be better.

1260
02:06:21,683 --> 02:06:24,723
However, only we will know that.

1261
02:06:29,748 --> 02:06:33,748
Bala, stay with her.

1262
02:06:35,746 --> 02:06:39,746
Malhun, you stay here too.

1263
02:06:42,014 --> 02:06:45,304
Tell everyone that my mother is dead.

1264
02:06:51,238 --> 02:06:53,558
Vizier will think she's dead.

1265
02:06:54,079 --> 02:06:58,079
He will die soon or later.

1266
02:07:09,453 --> 02:07:11,593
Look everywhere!

1267
02:07:11,613 --> 02:07:14,373
My Bey, how will you get out of here?

1268
02:07:14,631 --> 02:07:18,631
Don't worry, my Alps planned everything.

1269
02:07:18,794 --> 02:07:21,844
Listen to me carefully now.

1270
02:07:25,539 --> 02:07:31,469
That's why he'll set a
trap in the graveyard.

1271
02:07:32,156 --> 02:07:36,636
And he won't have any soldiers in Söğüt...

1272
02:07:37,305 --> 02:07:40,275
that will protect him from me.

1273
02:07:40,759 --> 02:07:46,839
I'll get you, Vizier Alemşah.

1274
02:07:54,384 --> 02:07:58,244
I will kill you here.

1275
02:08:05,919 --> 02:08:09,919
If Osman is not here now, he will come to
the graveyard anyway. (cemetery)

1276
02:08:19,910 --> 02:08:23,370
Ferman, let Geyhatu know.

1277
02:08:23,447 --> 02:08:26,317
Tell him Osman will come.

1278
02:08:28,521 --> 02:08:32,841
Celali and Konur, go to the graveyard.

1279
02:08:32,909 --> 02:08:37,009
Place a man everywhere. Osman
won't go out of the graveyard.

1280
02:08:37,303 --> 02:08:39,393
Don't worry.

1281
02:08:39,683 --> 02:08:42,873
We will bury Osman in his own grave.

1282
02:08:51,353 --> 02:08:53,673
Come, Osman.

1283
02:08:53,837 --> 02:08:59,467
I will bury you with
your loved one Selcan Mother.

1284
02:09:26,422 --> 02:09:29,332
Come, Vizier.

1285
02:10:02,753 --> 02:10:04,643
Osman.

1286
02:10:05,875 --> 02:10:08,265
Yes, Osman.

1287
02:10:11,023 --> 02:10:13,253
Osman.

1288
02:10:17,301 --> 02:10:23,851
You thought your sneaky plans would
go on, right, Vizier Alemşah?

1289
02:10:27,457 --> 02:10:31,197
I didn't have a sword, Osman.

1290
02:10:32,088 --> 02:10:39,108
You will be known as a traitor
when you kill me.

1291
02:10:52,650 --> 02:10:54,840
Soldiers!

1292
02:11:41,787 --> 02:11:46,417
You tried to make me a Sultan killer.

1293
02:11:47,941 --> 02:11:51,941
